&lt;h4&gt;Student Labs: Constructor Fabric Research Edition&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious how AI is changing the way software is built? Want to explore it hands-on, guided by the researchers who work on it every day?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Constructor Tech and Constructor Labs, together with Constructor University, invite you to &lt;strong&gt;Student Labs&lt;/strong&gt;: a 2-month educational research program for BSc and MSc students.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This edition is dedicated to &lt;strong&gt;Constructor Fabric&lt;/strong&gt;, a shared AI and software platform. Fabric brings together reusable building blocks, common infrastructure and AI agents that help design, build and test software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;🚀 Why Constructor Fabric?&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI-native software platforms are one of the &lt;strong&gt;fastest-growing fields in tech&lt;/strong&gt;, and few students get to study one from the inside. Student Labs gives you that chance. You explore open research questions on a platform in active development, learn current research methods, and build skills that are in high demand in industry and academia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;🔬 What you can research&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI that builds software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain-specific languages (DSL):&lt;/strong&gt; how a formal language can describe software components so that AI can generate and regenerate them from specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Neurosymbolic models:&lt;/strong&gt; combining neural networks with logic and rules, so that AI-generated code can be checked, not just produced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule extraction and fine-tuning:&lt;/strong&gt; how to extract rules and knowledge from existing code and use them to adapt language models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;World models:&lt;/strong&gt; how AI systems build an internal model of their environment to understand, plan and predict&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Formal verification:&lt;/strong&gt; mathematical methods that prove software behaves as specified&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geometric models:&lt;/strong&gt; using geometry to represent data and help AI models learn from it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benchmarking:&lt;/strong&gt; how to measure fairly whether one AI model or method is really better than another&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next-generation language models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diffusion models for text:&lt;/strong&gt; today’s LLMs write one token at a time, which makes them slow and prone to hallucinations. Diffusion models generate whole passages at once. Explore how to make them match and beat today’s models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LLM security:&lt;/strong&gt; how to host large language models securely when many users and organisations share the same system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;💡 What you’ll experience&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore an open research question that matches your level: beginner, intermediate or advanced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from weekly mentoring sessions with Constructor researchers and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exchange ideas with other students, and study solo or in a pair&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your results as a research report, prototype or research concept&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;🎓 Who can apply?&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc and MSc students of Constructor University and our partner universities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Students with a strong interest in AI, LLMs, software engineering or research. Beginners are welcome!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;👉 How it works&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choose a topic&lt;/strong&gt; from a curated list proposed by our researchers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Find your level.&lt;/strong&gt; Topics are offered for beginner, intermediate and advanced students, so everyone can find one that fits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Study solo or in a pair&lt;/strong&gt;, depending on the topic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead your own research&lt;/strong&gt; and set your own schedule, with weekly guidance from your mentor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Present your results&lt;/strong&gt; and receive feedback and a certificate of completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;⭐ Why join?&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Study a fast-growing field&lt;/strong&gt; from inside a real AI platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn from experts:&lt;/strong&gt; weekly mentorship from researchers and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Earn academic credit:&lt;/strong&gt; depending on your university’s rules, the Labs can count towards your mandatory internship, earn you project credits, or become part of your thesis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Publish:&lt;/strong&gt; strong results can be published, with you as an author&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build your research portfolio&lt;/strong&gt; and receive a certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps:&lt;/strong&gt; thesis co-supervision, and you can apply for paid internships in the Constructor ecosystem (separate application)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 &lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 months&lt;br&gt;📍 &lt;strong&gt;Format:&lt;/strong&gt; remote, or hybrid in Bremen (DE), Sofia (BG) or Belgrade (RS)&lt;br&gt;🗓 &lt;strong&gt;Mentoring:&lt;/strong&gt; weekly sessions with your mentor. About 10–15 hours a week; you set your own schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
