arder than it needs to be</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Contribute to our cross-team frontend architecture work — shared components,hooks and API clients, and how we render, test and ship our apps</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Keep merchant tooling fast — data-heavy tables, sales statistics and editorsare where perceived performance is won or lost</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Take on larger topics — an epic, a new integration, a new merchant surface —and break them down into something the team can execute: slices, dependencies, open questions, and a first piece worth shipping</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work in an agile cross-functional team with a product owner, designers and backend engineers, and connect what you build to merchant activation and conversion</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">What You´ll Bring</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Solid proficiency in TypeScript and React — component design, hooks, statemanagement, and the performance patterns that keep a growing app fast</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Around three or more years of professional experience building web products, with a track record of features you carried from first ticket to production</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Real CSS craft and experience working inside a design system or shared component library, not just against one</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience consuming REST or GraphQL APIs and working with structured, data-heavy responses — product catalogs, variants and attributes bring more complexity than they first appear to</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Working experience in a JVM backend — Kotlin or Java with Spring — and the ability to build a REST endpoint, model the data behind it and write the migration, not just read the code</s