"BulletListStyle1 SCXW217808204 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW217808204 BCX0">Vertrautheit mit <strong>Cloud-Plattformen wie AWS, GCP oder Azure</strong>, Containerisierung und Deployment von KI-Modellen&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW217808204 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW217808204 BCX0">Gute Kommunikationsfähigkeiten auf <strong>Deutsch und Englisch</strong>&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW217808204 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW217808204 BCX0">Lernbereitschaft, Teamfähigig und die Fähigkeit, komplexe technische Konzepte verständlich zu erklären&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW217808204 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW217808204 BCX0">Gute Projektmanagementfähigkeiten und die Fähigkeit, <strong>sowohl unabhängig als auch im Team</strong> zu arbeiten&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Über Machine Learning Reply</h3><p class="paragraph-01--light" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Machine Learning Reply bietet maßgeschneiderte End-to-End-Lösungen im Data-Science-Bereich an, die den gesamten Projektlebenszyklus abdecken – von der initialen Strategieberatung über die Datenarchitektur und Infrastrukturthemen bis hin zur Datenverarbeitung und Qualitätssicherung unter Verwendung von Machine-Learning-Algorithmen. Machine Learning Reply verfügt über umfassende Expertise im Bereich der Datenwissenschaft in allen Schlüsselindustrien der deutschen HDAX-Unternehmen. Machine Learning Reply befähigt seine Kunden, neue datenbasierte Geschäftsmodelle erfolgreich einzuführen sowie bereits bestehende Prozesse und Produkte zu optimieren – mit einem Schwerpunkt auf Open-Source- und Cloud-Technologien. Mit dem Machine Learning Incubator bietet das Unternehmen ein Programm zur Ausbildung der nächsten Generation von Entscheidungsträgern, Data Scientists und Entwicklern an.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/machine-learning-reply/genai-engineer-munich-83891","tags":["Data Science"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Munich, Bayern, Germany","created_at":1794637890},{"slug":"remote-senior-ai-product-designer-berlin-84714","company_name":"Recare Deutschland GmbH","title":"Senior AI Product Designer  (m/w/d)","description":"<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>About Recare</strong><br></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">As one of the leading German HealthTech companies, we are reshaping discharge management – technology-driven, patient-centered, and free from bureaucracy. In addition to our market-leading SaaS platform, we develop AI solutions that radically simplify processes in hospitals and for aftercare providers, relieve healthcare professionals, and refocus attention on patients. Today, we already connect two-thirds of all German hospitals with over 650 rehabilitation clinics and 25,000 nursing and homecare providers. With currently around 100 employees, we continue to grow – and we are looking for people with character who want to help us improve the healthcare system and solve administrative complexity across care journeys in Europe.<br><br></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>What you'll own as our Senior AI Product Designer</strong><br><br></p><ul><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You'll own end-to-end design for one of our core product areas, on a platform where AI is the foundation of the product, not a bolt-on feature. Your mission is to bring consumer-grade craft to a B2B healthcare product used by clinicians and hospital administrators under real time pressure, and to help invent the design patterns for AI-native surfaces that don't exist anywhere else yet.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You design the AI-native surfaces our platform is built around, including multi-modal interfaces, agent state, uncertainty, and human-in-the-loop controls, inventing the patterns as you go rather than adapting existing ones.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You own end-to-end design for a product area – Discharge Core, Voice Desktop, Extract &amp; Docs, Patient Overview, or Agent – taking work from a messy problem statement through to what ships in production.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You contribute to our design system, building the components and AI-specific conventions that other designers and teams build on.<br></p></li></ul><ul><li><p>You partner closely with product and engineering, shaping technical and product direction rather than being handed a spec to execute against.<br><br>You work with other designers across the organisation, bringing your input and influence beyond your own product area rather than staying inside a single team's boundary.<br></p></li></ul><ul><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You hold a high craft bar in critique, lifting the standard of what the wider design team ships.<br></p></li></ul><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You help hold coherence across our AI Suite (Voice, Docs, Extract, Agent) and Discharge Core, so a fast-growing multi-product platform still feels like one product to the people using it.<br><br></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>How we design:<br></strong></p><ul><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">We're AI-native. We use AI tools daily in our own process, not just in what we design, and we want strong, opinionated views on how to wield them well.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Consumer-grade craft is the bar, even in B2B. Our users are clinicians and hospital administrators.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Human-in-the-loop by default. This is healthcare: AI proposes, people stay in control, and we design the approval and verification moments that make that real, not just a confidence score bolted on.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">We ship in production, not just in Figma. Craft is judged by what clinicians actually use, so we stay close to what ships.<br></p></li></ul><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>What to expect as our Senior AI Product Designer (m/w/d):<br></strong></p><ul><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Purposeful work – your role will have a positive impact on patients, their families, and healthcare professionals.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Company culture – we believe in flat hierarchies that promote high performance and strong team dynamics. We foster an environment characterized by mutual respect, loyalty, and recognition. Together, we strive for our goals – and expect the same from you.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Flexibility – want to pick up your child from daycare? Like to exercise during lunch? We'll support you. We are a remote-friendly company offering flexible working hours. Workations are also possible by arrangement.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Edenred card – which you can use according to your needs.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Extra vacation day – so you can celebrate your birthday with your loved ones, you'll have the day off.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Here's how we picture you as our Senior AI Product Designer (m/w/d):<br></strong></p><ul><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You have 8+ years of product design experience, with at least 3+ years operating at Senior, Principal, or Staff altitude. <br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You have designed for AI and non-determinism before, and can talk concretely about how you've communicated agent behaviour, handled errors, and kept users in control, not just in the abstract.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You have owned or significantly contributed to a design system, at the level of patterns and principles rather than individual components.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You are block-shaped: equally strong across UX process, UI craft, product thinking, research, storytelling, and cross-functional collaboration.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You have taken features from 0 to 1 through an ambiguous problem statement to shipped code, and you're comfortable feeling like a PM or frontend developer on the days that calls for it.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You have high agency and spot gaps without being asked to look for them, including outside your own product area.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You hold a position under pressure but change it when new information warrants, rather than becoming precious about your own decisions.<br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You communicate confidently in English and are comfortable operating in an international environment; German is a plus but not required.</p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You bring a consumer-grade craft background with exceptional design; healthtech experience is a plus but not required.<br><br></p></li><li><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">If this sounds like your kind of challenge, we'd love to hear from you</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/recare-deutschland-gmbh/remote-senior-ai-product-designer-berlin-84714","tags":["Product","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1794637890},{"slug":"remote-software-engineer-computer-use-integrations-berlin-434731","company_name":"Recare Deutschland GmbH","title":"Software Engineer (Computer Use & Integrations) (m/w/d)","description":"<p><strong>Software Engineer – Backend (Computer Use &amp; Integrations) (m/w/d)<br></strong><br>Remote job</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About Recare</strong></p><p>As one of the leading German HealthTech companies, we are reshaping discharge management – technology-driven, patient-centered, and free from bureaucracy. In addition to our market-leading SaaS platform, we develop AI solutions that radically simplify processes in hospitals and for aftercare providers, relieve healthcare professionals, and refocus attention on patients. Today, we already connect two-thirds of all German hospitals with over 650 rehabilitation clinics and 25,000 nursing and homecare providers. With currently around 100 employees, we continue to grow – and we are looking for people with character who want to help us improve the healthcare system and solve administrative complexity across care journeys in Europe.</p><p><strong>What to expect as our Software Engineer – Backend (Computer Use &amp; Integrations) (m/w/d):</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Purposeful work</strong> – your role will have a positive impact on patients, their families, and healthcare professionals.</p></li><li><p><strong>Company culture</strong> – we believe in flat hierarchies that promote high performance and strong team dynamics. We foster an environment characterized by mutual respect, loyalty, and recognition. Together, we strive for our goals – and expect the same from you.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexibility</strong> – want to pick up your child from daycare? Like to exercise during lunch? We'll support you. We are a remote-friendly company offering flexible working hours. Workations are also possible by arrangement.</p></li><li><p><strong>Edenred card</strong> – which you can use according to your needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Extra vacation day</strong> – so you can celebrate your birthday with your loved ones, you'll have the day off.</p></li></ul><p><strong>In this role, you can make an impact and grow with us as Software Engineer <br></strong></p><p>You'll help build Recare's Operator, our agent that gets AI-generated clinical output into hospital systems by operating their existing software the way a person would, no bespoke interface required. It's the sharp end of our integration strategy: a Windows desktop application that automates UI interactions with hospital systems, running on doctors' devices and often inside RDP or Citrix environments. The first version is already live – you'll help expand its capabilities and make it reliable in production.</p><ul><li><p>You build and improve integrations between hospital systems and Recare products.</p></li><li><p>You implement and harden computer-use automation flows so they work reliably in production, including edge cases, recovery, and safety rails.</p></li><li><p>You partner with clinical domain experts to turn ambiguous workflows into shippable plans and robust implementations that solve real customers' needs.</p></li><li><p>You contribute across the stack as needed, including our Go-based gateway.</p></li><li><p>You invest in observability foundations (logs, metrics, traces) so we can trust the system in production.</p></li></ul><p><strong>How we work:<br></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>AI-native</strong> – our engineers reach for frontier coding agents every day to move fast across the whole stack, and we want strong, opinionated views on how to wield them well.</p></li><li><p><strong>Frontier models</strong> – we build on the best models available and adopt new capabilities as they ship, not a release later.</p></li><li><p><strong>Human-in-the-loop by default</strong> – this is healthcare: AI proposes, people stay in control, and we design the approval and validation loops that make that real.</p></li><li><p><strong>Unglamorous foundations</strong> – engineers get the time to build the eval harnesses, guardrails, and observability that make AI trustworthy in production, not just the feature on top.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ship and observe</strong> – always deployable, telemetry-driven, fix in the open.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>Here's how we picture you as our Software Engineer<br></strong></p><ul><li><p>You're a builder with a hacker mindset: you default to building rather than waiting, and you're solution-oriented rather than problem-oriented.</p></li><li><p>You have professional backend experience in Go, Python, or TypeScript, and you can point to production software you shipped and owned.</p></li><li><p>You're comfortable working on integration-heavy systems: APIs, workflows, data models, auth, and real-world edge cases.</p></li><li><p>You're pragmatic about reliability: you care about monitoring, debugging, test coverage, and making systems operable.</p></li><li><p>You're excited to use AI coding agents daily and have opinions on how to use them effectively.</p></li><li><p>You're ambitious but frustration-tolerant. Hospital IT is complicated and progress is hard-won; you stay relentless, get your hands dirty, and iterate until it works.</p></li><li><p>You communicate confidently in English and collaborate well across Product, Engineering, and Operations.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>German language skills.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Electron or TypeScript on the desktop side.</p></li><li><p>Experience with healthcare IT systems (HIS, KIS, PVS, EMR) and interoperability standards such as HL7 v2 or FHIR.</p></li></ul><p><br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/recare-deutschland-gmbh/remote-software-engineer-computer-use-integrations-berlin-434731","tags":["Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1794637890},{"slug":"remote-lead-security-engineer-berlin-229517","company_name":"Recare Deutschland GmbH","title":"Lead Security Engineer (m/w/d)","description":"<p><strong>Lead Security Engineer (m/w/d)<br><br></strong></p><p><strong>About Recare<br><br></strong>As one of the leading German HealthTech companies, we are reshaping discharge management – technology-driven, patient-centered, and free from bureaucracy. In addition to our market-leading SaaS platform, we develop AI solutions that radically simplify processes in hospitals and for aftercare providers, relieve healthcare professionals, and refocus attention on patients. Today, we already connect two-thirds of all German hospitals with over 650 rehabilitation clinics and 25,000 nursing and homecare providers. With currently around 120 employees from a broad range of nations, we continue to grow – and we're now going far beyond our core business, aiming to eliminate bureaucracy and admin in hospitals with a whole portfolio of AI products.<br><br></p><p><strong>What to expect as our Lead Security Engineer (m/w/d):<br><br></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Purposeful work</strong> – your role will have a positive impact on patients, their families, and healthcare professionals.</p></li><li><p><strong>Company culture</strong> – we believe in flat hierarchies that promote high performance and strong team dynamics. We foster an environment characterized by mutual respect, loyalty, and recognition. Together, we strive for our goals – and expect the same from you.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexibility</strong> – want to pick up your child from daycare? Like to exercise during lunch? We'll support you. We are a remote-friendly company offering flexible working hours. Workations are also possible by arrangement.</p></li><li><p><strong>Edenred card</strong> – which you can use according to your needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Extra vacation day</strong> – so you can celebrate your birthday with your loved ones, you'll have the day off.<br><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>In this role, you can make an impact and grow with us as Lead Security Engineer (m/w/d):<br><br></strong></p><p>You'll be our first dedicated security engineer: a senior IC with no team at the start. You join as Deputy CISO, report to our Director of Technology (currently acting CISO), and build security engineering from scratch. The baseline is already in place – ISO 27001, C5 Type II, regular penetration tests, and encryption in the product. AI is adding new surfaces: voice documentation, document generation, and agentic workflows. You build and own the security program, the tooling, and the security story we tell customers.<br></p><ul><li><p><strong>Vulnerability management</strong> – scanners and dependency updates across repos, plus the process that gets findings closed.</p></li><li><p><strong>Partner to Platform</strong> – review security-sensitive infrastructure decisions and explore options like customer-managed keys or HSMs. Platform still owns architecture.</p></li><li><p><strong>Certifications, technical side</strong> – control design and assessments for our ISO 27001 and C5 setup, the security case for a potential upcoming Class IIa medical device (MDR), and pentest scoping and follow-up, with regulation like the EU Cyber Resilience Act on the horizon. This is roughly a quarter to a third of the role, and we say it openly: for the right person in healthcare security, it's a draw, not a chore.</p></li><li><p><strong>Customer security</strong> – reusable docs, evidence, and AI-assisted questionnaires, so the tenth enterprise deal costs a fraction of the first. You join the call when a hospital CISO asks something new about our AI architecture.</p></li><li><p><strong>Incident response</strong> – process, runbooks, and escalation, and you lead when it's real. We're too small for a SOC, so you design on-call that fits a company our size. Product incidents and platform bugs have their own owners in engineering.</p></li><li><p><strong>Company-wide security</strong> – watch the threat landscape, turn this week's supply-chain mess into concrete actions, and set the baselines IT applies to devices and accounts.<br><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>How we work:<br><br></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>AI-native</strong> – our engineers use coding agents every day. Security should too: scanning, evidence, questionnaires.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI is also our attack surface</strong> – agent sandboxing, prompt injection, voice data, computer-use automation inside hospitals. We deal with security questions most companies will only meet in a few years.</p></li><li><p><strong>Human-in-the-loop by default</strong> – this is healthcare: AI proposes, people stay in control.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ship and observe</strong> – we ship continuously and debug from telemetry, including in the open when that's the fastest path.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>Here's how we picture you as our Lead Security Engineer (m/w/d):<br><br></strong></p><ul><li><p>You're a hands-on security engineer with 6+ years across software and security engineering, and you can point to a security program (or a big part of one) you've owned.</p></li><li><p>You've been the technical counterpart through at least one ISO 27001, C5, or SOC 2 certification cycle: you've designed controls, faced an auditor, and written the technical side of a Statement of Applicability. This is a hard requirement.</p></li><li><p>You've run vulnerability management somewhere real: scanners, dependency bots, triage, and the follow-through that gets things fixed.</p></li><li><p>You follow the security scene closely (podcasts, advisories, incident write-ups) and usually have an opinion on this week's incident before it reaches the news.</p></li><li><p>You're genuinely curious about AI security – both securing AI systems (agents, sandboxing, data flows) and using AI tooling to work at leverage.</p></li><li><p>You can talk to engineers, auditors, and hospital security teams in English without a slide deck translating for you.<br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>German language skills, since our customers and the C5 world are German-speaking.</p></li><li><p>Experience in healthcare or another regulated domain.</p></li><li><p>Offensive security experience.</p></li><li><p>Security certifications such as OSCP, CISSP, or similar.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/recare-deutschland-gmbh/remote-lead-security-engineer-berlin-229517","tags":["Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1794637890},{"slug":"remote-tech-lead-medical-coding-agents-berlin-279658","company_name":"Recare Deutschland GmbH","title":"Tech Lead (Medical Coding Agents) (m/w/d)","description":"<p><strong>About Recare<br><br></strong></p><p>As one of the leading German HealthTech companies, we are reshaping discharge management: technology-driven, patient-centered and free from bureaucracy. In addition to our market-leading SaaS platform, we develop AI solutions that radically simplify processes in hospitals and for aftercare providers, relieve healthcare professionals and refocus attention on patients. Today, we already connect two-thirds of all German hospitals with thousands of rehabilitation clinics, nursing and homecare providers. With around 100 employees, we continue to grow, and we’re looking for people with character who want to help us improve the healthcare system.<br><br><br></p><p><strong>What you’ll do as our Tech Lead (Medical Coding Agents) (m/w/d):<br></strong></p><p>German hospitals are paid a fixed amount per case, based on the codes assigned to it. Insurers dispute a share of the bills through an external medical audit, and the hospital can appeal when the audit cuts a bill. Recare is building medical coding agents to rebuild this chain: they read the case file, propose codes, assess audit findings and draft appeals. A subject matter expert reviews every result.</p><p>You’ll lead the technical development of this product. The role is about 80% hands-on building and 20% leading, and it grows with the platform into areas beyond billing.<br><br><br></p><ul><li><p><strong>Technical direction:</strong> set the architecture with the team across backend, frontend and a data model built on healthcare standards such as FHIR. Set the technical roadmap with the team and deliver on it predictably.</p></li><li><p><strong>Agent orchestration:</strong> design how models, deterministic rules and human review fit together. Work with our AI engineers on system design.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hands-on delivery:</strong> build the backend for cases, documents and long-running agent runs, including the append-only decision log that keeps every case audit-proof when an insurer challenges it months later.</p></li><li><p><strong>Product partnership:</strong> be the technical counterpart to the product manager and the subject matter experts on planning, specs and trade-offs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Production quality:</strong> own reliability, observability and security in a sensitive healthcare context, with an eval harness built from expert-reviewed cases as a CI gate.<br><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>How we work:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>AI coding agents:</strong> engineers use them every day and take responsibility for the code we ship. Product managers and designers prototype in our codebase too, and engineers review what goes to production.</p></li><li><p><strong>Human-in-the-loop:</strong> agents propose, the expert accepts, corrects or rejects, and every decision is logged with its evidence.</p></li><li><p><strong>Shipping:</strong> we release early to development partners and switch features on per hospital.</p></li><li><p><strong>Data protection:</strong> EU-only inference and no patient data in logs are hard constraints.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ownership:</strong> product owns what we build and why. The tech lead owns how it’s built and that it ships.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stack:</strong> TypeScript, Node.js and Go, Python for inference, Postgres, React, AWS Bedrock, Docker and Datadog.</p></li><li><p><strong>Success:</strong> measured in revenue hospitals keep, not in usage.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>What we’re looking for:<br></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Leadership:</strong> 6+ years of experience, including leading a small team.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hands-on with LLMs:</strong> you’ve built with LLMs yourself and understand where they fail: non-determinism, cost, latency and evaluation. You can design systems around them and challenge our AI engineers’ choices. Experience running an LLM or agent system in production is a strong plus, and strong personal projects count.</p></li><li><p><strong>Evals:</strong> you can answer “how did you know it was good enough?” with ground truth, regression tests and a clear taxonomy of error classes.</p></li><li><p><strong>Full-stack depth:</strong> you go deep across backend, frontend and data, and you commit code.</p></li><li><p><strong>Other people’s systems:</strong> you’re comfortable with asynchronous pipelines, legacy interfaces and code written by others. Hospital experience isn’t required.</p></li><li><p><strong>Communication:</strong> you explain decisions and trade-offs clearly in English in a remote team.</p></li><li><p><strong>Nice to have:</strong> German, as the catalogues, the coding rules and much of the work with our experts are in German; an ML background, including judgement on when fine-tuning pays off; retrieval and source attribution; healthcare data standards such as FHIR; regulation such as MDR and the EU AI Act.<br><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>What we offer<br></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Growth:</strong> we invest in each person’s development, whether that’s taking ownership of new projects, deepening your technical leadership or exploring new AI approaches, supported by a dedicated learning and development budget and regular feedback. If you grow, we grow.</p></li><li><p><strong>Purposeful work:</strong> your work has a real impact on patients, their families and healthcare professionals.</p></li><li><p><strong>Company culture:</strong> flat hierarchies, strong team dynamics and a culture of mutual respect, loyalty and recognition. English is our working language across a team of 20+ nationalities.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexibility:</strong> need to pick up your child from daycare or want to exercise at lunch? We support you, with fully remote work, flexible hours and workations by arrangement.</p></li><li><p><strong>Your setup:</strong> a work laptop plus a one-off budget to choose and keep your own accessories.</p></li><li><p><strong>Monthly benefit:</strong> €50 per month for vouchers or an Urban Sports Club membership (for employees in Germany).</p></li><li><p><strong>Birthday off:</strong> your birthday off to celebrate with your loved ones.</p></li><li><p><strong>Together:</strong> team meetups and company-wide events.<br><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Location</strong></p><p>We’re a remote team, and the role is fully remote within European time zones. We’re hiring in Germany, Austria, Spain, Italy, Portugal, the Netherlands and the United Kingdom.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/recare-deutschland-gmbh/remote-tech-lead-medical-coding-agents-berlin-279658","tags":["Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1794637889},{"slug":"legal-advisor-investment-products-frankfurt-am-main-319050","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Legal Advisor Investment Products","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarter in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is an international bank in <strong>Zurich</strong>. We are looking for a product specialist (m, f, d) as a</p><p><strong>Legal Advisor Investment Products  </strong></p><p>Your Tasks: </p><p>Participate in product structuring for German investors/ Develop, establish and maintain investment programs, managed accounts and structured products / Interface function to internal and external service providers / Liaise with custodians, administrators, portfolio managers, marketing, risk management, operations, legal counsels / Responsible for market openings and account openings with external counterparties / Work on board resolutions, shareholder notices and other legal documents / Management of documents / Project coordination.</p><p>Your Profile: </p><p>Bachelor or Master in Law / Experience in product management, product structuring and/or investment funds in general / Understanding the needs of German investors / Project management and analytical skills / Interest in legal and regulatory aspects as well as operational processes / Proactive, dynamic and results-oriented personality / Ability to work independently and as part of a team / Languages: German and English. </p><p>Your Contact:</p><p>He is available and pleased to take time for your professional career development. </p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/legal-advisor-investment-products-frankfurt-am-main-319050","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Frankfurt am Main","created_at":1794634232},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-fde-grafenwohr-bavaria-447557","company_name":"Pvminc","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE)","description":"&lt;h1&gt;Senior Forward Deployed Engineer&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Forward Deployed Software Engineer &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;On-Site:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Grafenwohr, Germany – &lt;strong&gt;ACTIVE TS/SCI Clearance required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Reports to:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Echo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Direct reports:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; None. Delta’s provide performance feedback on other engineers and participate in company peer mentorship program.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Travel:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; 0-10%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At PVM, we serve those who serve, as a Palantir ally for mission impact. We are a veteran-founded, Palantir Vanguard partner — and the only small business providing services in that tier. We help&amp;nbsp;our government partners tackle real problems in National Security, Readiness, and Space — not building shelfware.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job__description body&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE), you will build analytical dashboard features, support CI/CD pipeline tasks, and work within a structured agile environment alongside senior engineers and government stakeholders. You will operate in two-week sprint cycles, contributing to feature delivery from design through deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At our organization, an FDE takes ownership of their work — building reliable features, writing meaningful code, and ensuring each sprint increment is production-ready.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deliver front-end analytical dashboard views using Foundry’s Workshop/Slate application layer under guidance from senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support CI/CD pipeline configuration tasks, including build scripts, automated tests, and environment promotion workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement metric definitions and data transformations aligned to the Foundry Ontology to ensure consistent data interpretation across dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear technical documentation, including configuration notes, runbooks, and sprint artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in sprint planning, daily standups, sprint reviews, and demonstrations for government stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct testing and validation to confirm dashboards function correctly and data aligns with approved definitions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify integration issues, surface blockers early, and collaborate with senior engineers to resolve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support defect resolution and incremental enhancements to maintain stable operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:540,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:270,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;12&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Deep expertise with Palantir Foundry Ontology Manager, Workshop, Actions, Pipeline Builder, and operational application development&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:60}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python, TypeScript, or Java in cloud-based data platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in government, defense, or classified environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently build features, test them, and deliver production-ready functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in small, fast-moving technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;•&quot; data-font=&quot;&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:540,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:270,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;•&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;17&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Experience conducting ontology reviews, governance assessments, and platform architecture evaluations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About PVM &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PVM, we mean it when we say we value diversity. As a PVM team member, you will work with people from all different backgrounds that are passionate about the problems we solve for our customers and are focused on delivering value for our clients. Our culture encourages problem solving, leadership, and innovation, and creates an environment that will support your professional and personal growth. Here are a few highlights of the advantages of being a part of the PVM community:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for growth and advancement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition/Training reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Peer bonus program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote and on-site positions available&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PVM delivers digital services that help government agencies unlock the power of their data for good and maximize the value of their technology investments. We design, develop, and deploy solutions to solve mission-critical problems. PVM is a black- and service-disabled veteran-owned small business and was founded by a retired Naval officer out of frustration with the status quo with one goal in mind: to help his fellow Shipmates solve the problems they were facing every day. Today, we continue to be driven by that same goal and are focused on taking on our clients’ missions as our own to make a difference in the communities we serve. PVM believes in equal opportunity employment. We won&#39;t discriminate against any employee or applicant based on race, gender, nationality, age, religion, disability, military status, or sexual orientation. As a company and as individuals, we&#39;re committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for our team, our family members, and our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-alert job-alert--margin&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;PVM, Inc. is an SBA 8(a)-certified, Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business and Palantir USG Vanguard Partner. PVM is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/pvminc/forward-deployed-engineer-fde-grafenwohr-bavaria-447557","tags":["Palantir Engineer Services"],"job_types":[],"location":"Grafenwohr, Bavaria","created_at":1794628535},{"slug":"senior-full-stack-engineer-experimentation-product-analytics-germany-remote-250355","company_name":"grafanalabs","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer | Experimentation - Product Analytics | Germany | Remote","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote opportunity and we would be interested in applications from the UK, Ireland, Sweden, Spain and Germany.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is building a native experimentation platform: a Grafana app that lets teams define A/B tests, connect them to feature flags and product telemetry, and get trustworthy, statistically sound answers about what their changes actually did.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It started as a hackathon project and is now used by Grafana engineering and product teams in our internal environment to run real experiments. The next step is to make it a first-class product: one we rely on every day internally and, over time, one we offer to Grafana Cloud customers alongside Frontend Observability, Session Replay and our other user-experience capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the &lt;strong&gt;Product Analytics team&lt;/strong&gt;, a group of highly technical product analysts who help teams across Grafana understand how our products are used and run experiments on them. As the team&#39;s dedicated software engineer, you&#39;ll own the engineering of the experimentation app and have a lot of influence over where it goes. You&#39;ll partner closely with data scientists on the statistics, data engineers on event pipelines and the data warehouse, software engineers across Grafana on feature flags, Frontend Observability and the App Platform, and product stakeholders who rely on experiment results to make decisions. This is a hands-on engineering role that ships production code. It is not an analyst role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the product:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The experimentation app is built on the Grafana App Platform:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; a TypeScript and React app plugin using @grafana/ui, plus a custom datasource plugin that powers experiment statistics panels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; Go, built with the Grafana App SDK. Experiments are Kubernetes-style custom resources defined in CUE, with an operator, admission webhooks, and support for declarative, GitOps-style management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature flags:&lt;/strong&gt; integration with &lt;strong&gt;OpenFeature&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;OpenFeature Remote Evaluation Protocol (OFREP)&lt;/strong&gt;, Grafana&#39;s multi-tenant feature toggle service, and an embedded GO Feature Flag evaluator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statistics engine:&lt;/strong&gt; a Bayesian analysis engine (TypeScript, with a Go port) that produces a direction-aware verdict per metric, probability to be best, credible intervals, expected loss and sample-size recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data:&lt;/strong&gt; experiment exposure and outcome events flow from product instrumentation through RudderStack into BigQuery, or from Grafana Faro into Loki, and are queried live through Grafana datasources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI:&lt;/strong&gt; experiment authoring assisted by &lt;strong&gt;Grafana Assistant&lt;/strong&gt;, which discovers relevant data and drafts the experiment configuration for a human to review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve the experimentation app from internal tool to product.&lt;/strong&gt; Full ownership of features end to end across the React frontend and Go backend, from problem framing and design through rollout, measurement and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the experimentation experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop intuitive workflows for defining hypotheses, configuring experiments and metrics, managing their lifecycle, and exploring results. Make these experiences useful for product managers and analysts as well as engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make instrumentation easier to adopt and trust&lt;/strong&gt;. Evolve the experimentation SDK and its OpenFeature and Faro integrations. Help teams connect variant assignment, actual exposure, and outcome events with consistent identity and event contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect experiments to the rest of Grafana’s user-experience stack.&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate with Grafana Faro and Frontend Observability so flag exposures and outcomes are captured automatically, and link experiment results to Session Replay and critical user journeys so teams can see &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; a variant won, not only &lt;em&gt;that&lt;/em&gt; it won.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harden the statistics and analysis path.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with our data analysts to extend the statistics engine, and make analysis scalable, cost-aware and correct. Examples include moving computation server-side, scheduled analysis, alerting on experiment health, and guardrails against misleading results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI where it genuinely helps.&lt;/strong&gt; Extend the Grafana Assistant integration for authoring, explaining and reporting on experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Mentor teammates, including analysts who contribute code, through code review, pairing and design docs. Write the architecture decision records (ADRs), docs and demos that help other teams adopt experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own what you ship.&lt;/strong&gt; Take part in on-call for the services you build, and support the internal teams that run experiments on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest heavily in developer productivity. You can use modern AI coding assistants as part of your daily workflow (your choice of tools, within security guidelines), backed by a company-funded usage budget so you can iterate quickly without unnecessary friction. We encourage pragmatic AI-assisted development: faster prototyping, test generation, refactors, documentation, and incident follow-ups, always with strong code review and quality standards. You’ll also have access to the latest frontier models from OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes you a great fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We highly value people who are intellectually curious, default to transparency, have a strong bias towards action, and are kind and enjoy working as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong full-stack engineering experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve built and operated production web applications with TypeScript and React, and backend services in Go (or a similar language, with willingness to work in Go). You value maintainability, automated testing and secure development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building an in-house platform or integrating existing experimentation and A/B testing platform &lt;/strong&gt;(for example Statsig, Eppo, GrowthBook, Optimizely, LaunchDarkly experiments, or an in-house platform).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product and data intuition.&lt;/strong&gt; You care whether what you shipped actually moved the needle, and you’re comfortable working with event data, SQL and data warehouses such as BigQuery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve delivered complex projects with minimal supervision, broken them into short feedback loops (analyze, design, ship an MVP, learn, iterate), and helped teammates work more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational responsibility.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve been on call, supported software in production, and know how to make systems observable and debuggable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pragmatic AI usage.&lt;/strong&gt; You use AI coding tools thoughtfully, validate their output, and share practices that improve the team’s speed &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communication.&lt;/strong&gt; You can explain technical and statistical tradeoffs to engineers, analysts and product managers in a fully remote, asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with feature flags and OpenFeature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of experiment statistics: Bayesian or frequentist testing, sample sizing, variance reduction, and common pitfalls such as peeking and sample ratio mismatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes concepts: custom resources, operators, admission webhooks, GitOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building Grafana plugins or apps, or with the Grafana App SDK or Scenes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with frontend observability and product analytics tooling, such as Grafana Faro, RUM, session replay, RudderStack or Segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open source contribution or maintainership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a user of Grafana, Prometheus, Loki or Tempo, whether at work or on a homelab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Germany, the base compensation range for this role is €&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;100,000 - €125,000&lt;/span&gt;. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
