 style="min-height:1.5em">We value and celebrate our diverse culture. You are welcome here for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or whether you prefer bar graphs to pie charts. Your story matters – keep writing it as part of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to join us?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role</strong><br /><br />As a (Junior) Graphic Designer in our Licensing Team at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://rankings.statista.com/en/">Statista R</a>, you will work closely with Sales and Project Management to create effective, on-brand marketing and licensing materials. This is a great opportunity to build hands-on experience across print design, digital assets, brand implementation, and AI-supported design workflows.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and develop sales and licensing materials, including brochures, cover letters, order forms, certificates, and presentation assets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create premium quality seals and award badges that reflect the credibility and high standards of our rankings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle layout, final artwork, file preparation, and the creation of print-ready PDFs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Edit and optimize images for print and digital use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve and further develop existing sales collateral using innovative design methods and AI-powered creative tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design merchandise and promotional materials, such as stickers, roll-ups, and additional point-of-sale assets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure all materials align with corporate design guidelines and maintain a consistent