s of care teams and patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the next phases of the multi-year authentication migration to a self-hosted, Keycloak-based identity provider — completing token-based sign-in for Doctolib Pro apps and making the identity provider the single source of truth for user data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the reliability of high-traffic authentication systems end-to-end: monitoring, alerting, SLOs, incident resolution, post-mortems, and safe rollout practices (feature flags, canary releases, zero-downtime migrations)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive cross-team delivery independently: produce design documents and decision memos, build alignment across dependent teams, and make trade-offs explicit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with the Product Security team on security-sensitive architecture decisions and changes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to frontend development in React and TypeScript on the custom interfaces tied to the IAM platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI tools daily to accelerate your own work and help establish repeatable AI-augmented workflows across the team</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before you read on: if you don't have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll be a great fit if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have 7–10+ years of backend engineering experience with hands-on, daily Java or Kotlin development and a solid understanding of JVM internals (garbage collection, memory management, multi-threading, and profiling)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have proven experience building and operating high-traffic production systems at scale — load testing, capacity planning, horizontal scaling, caching, and performance bottleneck identification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own reliability end-to-end: you define monitoring, alerting, and SLOs, lead incident resolution, write post-mortems, and have shipped changes safely via feature flags, canary releases, and zero-downtime migrations on live systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have led complex, multi-week cross-team delivery independently — producing design docs, driving alignment across dependent teams, and making trade-offs explicit without waiting for consensus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI tools daily in your engineering workflow, critically validate their outputs, and are excited to help establish shared AI practices for your team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are fluent in English (written and spoken)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>It would be fantastic if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have prior experience with identity providers (e.g. Keycloak), OAuth2, and/or OIDC</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have hands-on experience with security practices for exposed, high-traffic endpoints</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have contributed to frontend codebases in React and TypeScript</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have exposure to Kafka/CDC</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have exposure to mobile authentication</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Life at Doctolib Tech</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our solutions are built on a single fully cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile app interfaces, multiple languages, and is adapted to country and healthcare specialty requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our stack is composed of Rails, TypeScript, Java, Python, Kotlin, Swift, and React Native.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We leverage AI ethically across our products to empower patients and health professionals. Discover our AI vision<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/"> <u>here</u></a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to learn more about our tech culture and environment? Visit the</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.doctolib.com/tech-doctolib/"><em> <u>Doctolib Tech site</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><h3></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Deutschlandticket (Germany-wide public transport pass) fully paid for by Doctolib</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">28 vacation days + 1 additional day for each full calendar year of employment (up to a maximum of 30 days)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad for up to 10 days per year thanks to our flexibility days policy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company health insurance with great supplementary benefits through our partner Allianz</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company pension scheme (bAV) through Allianz with an employer subsidy of 40% (15% within the probationary period)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Doctolib Parent Care program, which includes one month additional parental leave and much more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enrollment in Doctolib's long-term employee value sharing plan called DoctoGrowth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free mental health and coaching services through our partner <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Moka.care">Moka.care</a></p></li><li><p style="min-hei