&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our Mobile Engineering discipline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mobile engineers have a variety of different backgrounds&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are ~60 Android engineers at Monzo and we’re looking for more to join the team. We have several non-graduates; only some of us studied Computer Science; some of us have worked in huge companies; some have only ever worked in startups; others are former consultants. As long as you enjoy learning new things, we’d love to talk to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Monzo works in small, interdisciplinary teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have around 600 engineers out of roughly 5,000 people in total - and we have big ambitions. There are many interesting challenges ahead, and we&#39;re happy for people to move between teams or to specialise, whatever you prefer. As an engineer here you&#39;d be able to work directly with anyone across the company, and we run regular knowledge-sharing sessions so you’ll learn heaps about everything from how banks work to effective communication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day-to-day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re searching for &lt;strong&gt;product-focused Android engineers&lt;/strong&gt; to evolve our native mobile app.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll take pride in building polished user experiences, and you’ll balance the need for well-tested resilient code with moving fast and iterating.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be working on a product that is a part of day to day life for more than 15 million people already, and your work here will shape the way that people interact with their finances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Android Engineer at Monzo you&#39;ll work in a small, autonomous product squad alongside iOS Engineers, Backend Engineers, User Researchers, Product Designers, Product Managers, QA Testers, and Data Scientists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You and your team will be responsible for an overall company goal, rather than building a specific feature - you&#39;ll have the opportunity to have impact on both &lt;em&gt;what&lt;/em&gt; we build, and &lt;em&gt;how&lt;/em&gt; we build it. Mobile engineers at Monzo work on everything from the personal banking product to customer support tools. We also have a small mobile platform squad dedicated to enabling other engineers to move faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every week we meet as an Android discipline to discuss tools, techniques, problems we&#39;re encountering across the company and work together to improve our codebase and processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to an engineering manager who will meet with you every 1-2 weeks 1:1. They’re dedicated to helping you grow and develop as an engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Android app&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our app is 100% Kotlin, built using MVVM (Model View ViewModel) and Coordinators, and modularised by product feature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Around 95% of the codebase is in Compose. We use Coroutines, Retrofit and Moshi for API calls and Metro for dependency injection. Room is our choice for persistence, and we use repositories for interacting with data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use GitHub Pull Requests to do code reviews, and write unit tests for our ViewModels, Coordinators, and any other classes which contain logic. We write tests for all of our Compose screens and snapshot test them with Happo. We also use Espresso to test flows, which are executed via our continuous integration system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve previously written about &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/2019/02/11/building-monzo-chat-on-android&quot;&gt;building Monzo Chat&lt;/a&gt; on Android, which goes into detail on some of these elements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You should apply if&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about the impact your work has on our customers, and optimise for outcomes rather than the number of lines of code you output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited about and have experience in programming in Kotlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve shipped and iterated on at least one app in the Play Store&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a product mindset: you care about customer outcomes and you want to make data-informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love turning excellent design into beautiful products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable working in a team that deals with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an understanding computer science principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Interview Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our interview process involves three main stages:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial Call&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take home task or pair coding exercise&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final interview including a system design and a behavioural interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our average process takes around 2-3 weeks but we will always work around your availability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the chance to speak to our recruitment team at various points during your process but if you do have any specific questions or want to talk through reasonable adjustments ahead of or during application please us at any point on ----- &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please also use that email to let us know if there&#39;s anything we can do to make your application process easier for you, because of disability, neurodiversity or any other personal reason.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There’s a detailed blog on &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/2022/03/22/preparing-for-mobile-interviews-at-monzo&quot;&gt;the interview process&lt;/a&gt;, for extra details, hints and tips.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work 💻:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Locations &amp;amp; Flexible Working :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our main tech hub is in London, but our engineers live everywhere in the UK— from Brighton to the Western Isles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value meeting in person but there’s no pressure to come into the office, even if you&#39;re nearby. We believe you&#39;ll do your best work if you are where you want to be. If you live outside of London and we ask you to come into the office, Monzo will support you with the costs. ✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are naturally social, especially Tuesdays, Wednesdays and Thursdays, which happen to line up with our twice-weekly Monzo lunches &amp;amp; treat Thursdays 🍽️. Teams also schedule time together often for work and play – in or around the office, or online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set up a work schedule that delivers impact and fits your life.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Monzo, we value connections, flexibility, and wellbeing. We keep our meetings during core hours to stay connected and believe in maintaining work/life balance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be empowered to manage your work in a way that suits you and your team, giving you the freedom for children drop-offs and pick-ups, walking your dog or adventurous cat, avoiding peak commuting times or gym slots, appointments, or supporting your family in an emergency. 🕒✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work the way that works for you with Monzo! 💼&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What’s in it for you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 £78,000 - £110,000 base salary per year &lt;em&gt;+ &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Incentive Awards tied to your performance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;+&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt; Benefits&lt;/a&gt;, we also provide all of our engineers with the latest MacBook Pro.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;✈️We can help you relocate to the UK&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;✅We can sponsor visas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍This role can be based in our London office, but we&#39;re open to distributed working within the UK (with ad hoc meetings in London).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⏰ We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, at times that suit you and your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 Learning budget of £1,000 a year for books, training courses and conferences&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➕ And much more, see our full list of benefits&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/monzoreferrals/android-engineer-cardiff-370581","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Cardiff","created_at":1794639320},{"slug":"research-engineer-london-151286","company_name":"Genomics","title":"Research Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: </strong>Oxford or London (Hybrid)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Mission: Why We Exist</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genomics is a science-led transatlantic TechBio combining large-scale genetic and health data with proprietary analytics to accelerate drug discovery and advance predictive, preventative healthcare. We are united by a single vision to help people live longer healthier lives, using the power of genomics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genomics aims to help people live longer, healthier lives in two ways: super-charging drug discovery and development for novel treatments with our AI-enabled advanced genetic analytics platform, and by helping people understand their personal risk of common chronic diseases through polygenic risk scores - giving doctors and health systems the chance to get the right people into the right prevention, screening and treatment programmes at the right time.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3>Role Purpose</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an exceptional Research Engineer with strong computational skills and a track record of applying them to large-scale data science. A background in human genetics is preferred, but if you come from another quantitative field and are excited by the potential of genetics to transform healthcare, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join a team of experts in human genetics, data science and software engineering, building the platform at the heart of our Life Sciences work – (1) helping us derive new insights into human biology and guide drug development towards safer, more effective targets; (2) providing our SaaS customers with innovative analytics. How your time splits across methodology, software engineering and analysis will reflect your own balance of computational and scientific strengths.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role can be hired at IC2 (Research Engineer) or IC3 (Senior Research Engineer) level, depending on your experience. At IC3, you'll operate with greater autonomy, hold a broader technical scope, bring deeper subject-matter expertise, and lead projects that require integrated updates across multiple tools, working with cross-disciplinary teams to deliver value.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>A Day in the Life</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of this role is the opportunity to collaborate with domain experts at the cutting edge of statistical genetics and rapidly translate their innovations into a mature, integrated data &amp; analytics engine for commercial use at scale.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help expand and maintain our in-house Life Sciences tools and pipelines, planning your own work and contributing code to a shared codebase alongside Research Engineering team members, Software Engineers and Data Scientists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement algorithms developed within our Life Sciences teams to a high standard of robustness, testing and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run high-quality analyses of large-scale biological datasets using existing or bespoke tools, and share your findings with scientists and other stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to internal and external presentations and publications arising from our work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep your knowledge current on innovation and good practice in genomics, data science and scientific computing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Senior (IC3) level, you'll also lead projects that need integrated updates across multiple tools, coordinating with cross-disciplinary teams to deliver value.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Who You Are</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Essential</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong quantitative background in a scientific field, with the ability to explain complex ideas to specialists and non-specialists alike.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skilled at writing high-quality Python code using modern software development practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident analysing and learning from large-scale datasets in a scientific context.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experienced running tools and workflows in a scalable system, for example Linux based HPC environments or on cloud systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable using LLM programming assistants appropriately within a research software environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">It'd be great if you also have</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working on a collaborative codebase using version control and CI/CD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with common bioinformatics and genomics tools and file formats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and running large-scale workflows, e.g. WDL, CWL.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in remote, cloud-based environments, e.g. AWS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience creating and working with containers, e.g. Docker, Singularity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional programming languages, particularly R or C++.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A PhD or postgraduate degree in a scientific field, ideally genomics, bioinformatics or computational biology, with familiarity in statistics and machine learning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience working in a team, ideally in an industry setting.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Package</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to providing a transparent, supportive, and rewarding work environment.</p><h3><strong>Compensation &amp; Growth</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive Salary</strong>: Salaries are externally benchmarked annually to ensure competitive compensation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear Career Path:</strong> A straightforward, open progression framework means you'll always know the path to promotion and how to achieve your next career goal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> Including external courses and a wide library of L&amp;D materials, because your growth is our success.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Wellbeing &amp; Time Off</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Holiday:</strong> 25 days annual leave, plus bank holidays, plus an extra 3-day company-wide shutdown at year-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial &amp; Health Security:</strong> Robust benefits including a market-leading pension scheme, comprehensive private health insurance for you and your family with NO excess, critical illness, and life assurance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced Leave</strong>: Enhanced paid family leave to support all new parents.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Work Environment &amp; Culture</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible Working:</strong> Hybrid Working (e.g., From our London, Oxford Office)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Truly Inclusive Time Off:</strong> Our 'Bank Your Bank Holiday' program allows you to exchange public holidays for dates that hold personal or cultural significance to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vibrant Social Culture:</strong> From regular Town Halls and team picnics to organised sports events, our social committee ensures frequent opportunities to connect and celebrate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Green Commute:</strong> Cycle-to-Work scheme and convenient office locations near major transport hubs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to Build the Future?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this opportunity excites you, <strong>apply now!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are dedicated to creating a diverse environment and are proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genomics politely requests no contact from recruitment agencies. We do not accept speculative CVs from recruitment agencies nor accept the fees associated with them.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/genomics/research-engineer-london-151286","tags":["Science Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794638432},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-onboard-services-london-73714","company_name":"Uforce","title":"Staff Software Engineer (Onboard Services)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>About the role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Staff Software Engineer (Onboard Services) will design, build, and operate the software services that run on UFORCE’s uncrewed vehicles — spanning video streaming, telemetry, autonomy integration, vehicle control, health monitoring, navigation, and device integrations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will turn independently evolved services into one secure, testable, and maintainable onboard platform. This is a hands-on software engineering role focused on production Python services, service architecture, messaging, and reliable operation on constrained Linux hardware, including Raspberry Pi, x86, and NVIDIA Jetson.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also own the boundary between the vehicle and the backend: clear, versioned contracts with cloud services, deployment systems, video infrastructure, and operator interfaces that work over intermittent, low-bandwidth links. Working with backend, autonomy, hardware, QA, and field teams, you will make releases predictable and catch failures on the bench, not in the field.</p><h3>What you’ll do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and evolve a unified onboard service architecture: service boundaries, messaging, configuration, startup ordering, readiness, watchdogs, and graceful degradation when dependencies or devices are unavailable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and migrate production services to shared patterns, using reusable libraries and a reference service template covering project structure, packaging, logging, health reporting, and lifecycle management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standardise local service communication around NATS, with clear rules for integrating MAVLink, ZMQ IPC, and HTTP where appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design stable, versioned vehicle-to-backend contracts for telemetry, commands and acknowledgements, video metadata and control, configuration, health, and logs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineer for unreliable connectivity: buffering and store-and-forward, idempotent commands, explicit acknowledgements and timeouts, reconnection, back-off, and safe behaviour when the backend is unreachable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement secure-by-default services: least-privilege identities and messaging permissions, mutually authenticated and encrypted backend links, secure credential provisioning and rotation, sandboxed runtimes, and audit events for safety-critical commands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen automated testing across unit, contract, integration, simulation, and hardware-in-the-loop tests, with CI gates that catch regressions before release.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build safer release workflows with signed packages, dependency scanning, bench smoke and soak tests, staged fleet rollouts, and reliable rollback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profile services and enforce practical CPU, memory, and latency budgets on target hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve field diagnostics through structured logs, metrics, standardised health reporting, post-mission log capture, and actionable runbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document architectural decisions and service interfaces, communicate trade-offs clearly, and use AI coding tools to accelerate delivery without compromising quality.</p></li></ul><h3>What success looks like</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively developed onboard services converge on a shared architecture, supported Python runtime, messaging model, and service template.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineers can take a new service from an empty repository to running on a bench vehicle in a day or less, with less duplicated infrastructure code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vehicle-to-backend contracts remain compatible as cloud and vehicle software evolve at different speeds, preventing integration failures in the field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Authentication, least privilege, secret handling, runtime hardening, and supply-chain checks are consistently applied across the onboard stack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automated tests and bench validation catch defects before deployment, reducing issues discovered in the field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Releases move predictably from bench validation to pilot vehicles and the wider fleet, with clear readiness gates and rollback procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Services stay within resource budgets and remain diagnosable under hardware constraints and degraded connectivity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architecture documentation and runbooks help engineering, QA, and field teams integrate changes and resolve failures faster.</p></li></ul><h3>Required Qualifications</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>10+ years of professional experience in software engineering</strong>, delivering and operating production systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2+ years as a Tech Lead or Staff Engineer</strong>, owning architecture across multiple services or teams and establishing standards adopted by others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expert Python</strong> — designs and ships production services (asyncio, packaging, testing, profiling, and performance); <strong>Node.js</strong> experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Distributed / edge system architecture</strong> — has designed service architectures and messaging systems (e.g., NATS, MQTT, ZMQ, Kafka) with versioned contracts across system boundaries and unreliable networks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Web development and API experience</strong> — has built and evolved HTTP/WebSocket APIs and message-based integrations for multiple consumers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Security architecture</strong> — has led the design of authentication and authorisation, secrets and key management, secure updates, and supply-chain controls; security reviews or certification evidence are a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality engineering leadership</strong> — has established test strategies, CI gates, and staged release pipelines for a team or organisation; simulator or hardware-in-the-loop experience is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Development with AI tools</strong> — uses AI coding assistants or agents daily and has introduced practices that help a team use them effectively and safely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>C++, Rust, or Go</strong> experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>UxV, robotics, or embedded/edge Linux experience</strong> (e.g., MAVLink, GStreamer, serial/CAN devices, systemd services on constrained hardware) is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/staff-software-engineer-onboard-services-london-73714","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom - London","created_at":1794638432},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-nova-core-london-128331","company_name":"Uforce","title":"Senior Software Engineer (Nova Core)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>About the role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Senior Software Engineer (Nova Core) will design, build, and operate the backend services and platform foundations that enable reliable, secure, and maintainable C2 operations across Nova Cloud deployments. This role focuses on the Nova Core “inner loop”: service architecture, APIs, data models, persistence, authn/authz, observability, and developer experience that other Nova modules and product teams depend on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What you’ll do</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Own and ship critical Nova Core backend services (e.g., common APIs, configuration service, tenant/environment lifecycle, shared domain libraries). </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Design stable, backward-compatible API contracts (schemas, versioning, deprecation/migration playbooks) to protect dependent services and teams. • Build and evolve data models and persistence layers, including schema evolution, migrations, correctness guarantees, and safe rollout strategies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Establish production-grade operability: structured logging, metrics, tracing, dashboards, and actionable alerts; write and maintain runbooks. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Improve reliability over time by reducing incident frequency and driving down MTTD/MTTR through instrumentation and post-incident improvements. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Implement secure-by-default backend patterns (least privilege, secret management, audit events, policy hooks) and make them reusable across teams. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Contribute to and enforce consistent RBAC/permissions and authorization checks across services and APIs. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Add security-focused tests and CI/CD gates informed by threat modeling to reduce regressions. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Build and maintain shared backend libraries/SDKs with strong documentation and examples to accelerate adoption and reduce duplicated work. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Improve developer experience: faster local workflows, environment parity (e.g., dockerized deps, seeded data), and rapid test feedback. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Strengthen test harnesses (contract tests, integration tests, performance baselines) to catch cross-service breakages earlier. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Diagnose and fix high-impact performance bottlenecks (latency hot paths, caching, concurrency, DB query efficiency) and introduce pragmatic performance budgets. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Refactor brittle areas and pay down targeted technical debt to improve maintainability and reduce operational risk. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Communicate trade-offs clearly and collaborate effectively with dependent engineering and product teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What success looks like</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Core Nova services are delivered, adopted, and operated reliably with clear SLIs/SLOs and runbooks. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Observability is strong enough that incidents are detected quickly and resolved faster over time (improving MTTD/MTTR). </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• API versioning and compatibility practices reduce integration churn and prevent breaking changes for dependent teams. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Security and access-control foundations (authn/authz, auditability, secret handling, least privilege) are consistently applied across Nova Core services. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Shared contracts, libraries, and SDKs meaningfully reduce duplicated service work and accelerate delivery across Nova modules. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• CI/CD and release processes enable safer, more frequent deployments of core services. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Performance and correctness improve measurably in critical workflows (latency, resource usage, query efficiency, failure handling). </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Technical debt is paid down in targeted areas, improving maintainability and reducing operational risk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Required Qualifications</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">• 5+ years building and operating production backend systems and services. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Strong experience in API design, backend architecture, and evolving contracts safely over time. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Solid data modeling and persistence experience (SQL and/or NoSQL), including migrations and schema evolution. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Demonstrated operational ownership: observability, on-call readiness, incident response, and production debugging. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Security-