rt of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Staff Software Engineer (Autonomy) will design, build, and operate software capabilities that improve the mission effectiveness and safety of uncrewed surface vehicles across the UFORCE C2/C4ISR stack.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role spans <strong>Perception Autonomy, Autonomy Behaviours</strong>—including collision avoidance (COLAV), target-based manoeuvring and engagement—and <strong>Swarm Intelligence</strong>. You will take cross-system initiatives from design and implementation through scenario-based verification, field trials, deployment, and iteration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role requires strong software engineering and mathematical foundations, with an emphasis on autonomy that remains safe, observable, and useful in real operating conditions—including degraded sensors, different sea states, and GNSS- or RF-challenged environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What you’ll do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build production-grade capabilities across perception, autonomous behaviours, COLAV, and multi-USV coordination.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define measurable acceptance criteria for autonomy performance, safety, reliability, and operator trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate perception and behaviours across day/night operations, different sea states, sensor degradation, and GNSS/RF-challenged conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop swarm capabilities such as task allocation, role assignment, formation control, and distributed sensing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build scenari