ram an accountable program manager or execution owner, and build a team that solves problems itself and does not simply report status.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a service model that supports global and regional priorities without becoming a decision-making bottleneck.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reduce duplicated work and unnecessary coordination overhead across teams, and improve how predictably major initiatives are delivered.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have personally led several high-priority, cross-functional initiatives from ambiguous requirements to successful delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built, scaled, or materially improved a PMO or enterprise program management function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have managed programs across multiple countries, business units, or distributed organisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have worked directly with C-level executives and functional leaders to set priorities, resolve conflicts, and drive execution without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have managed competing initiatives and limited resources across a portfolio of programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have managed and developed program managers or similar cross-functional execution teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have put practical tracking, executive reporting, and accountability systems in place that improved delivery outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have worked in a fast-growing organisation with a lot of ambiguity and changing structures, and can move between portfolio-level prioritisation and detailed execution.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in hardware, manufacturing, defence, government technology, or another complex delivery environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A professional services background, or experience in a complex enterprise with heavy cross-functional dependencies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/remote-global-pmo-lead-246365","tags":["Strategy / Biz Ops"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom | Remote","created_at":1794638432},{"slug":"business-development-associate-investor-network-united-kingdom-424003","company_name":"Pairs","title":"Business Development Associate – Investor Network","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring an associate to build and run their own book of investors who back startups directly, and to introduce those investors to the founders we work with.<br /><br /><strong>About Pairs</strong><br />Pairs is a vetted private capital network. We put breakout US founders, from seed to Series B, in front of the family offices, VCs and strategic investors who know their market and can open the doors they need. We work only with the top 1% of deals, vet every founder and investor before they join, and invest our own money alongside our investors in a few of the companies we believe in most.<br /><br /><strong>The role</strong><br />You grow the investor side of Pairs. Your book is made of the investors you bring with you and the ones you open here, you keep those relationships warm, and you book the meetings between our founders and the investors who fit them. Family offices and private wealth are the investors we most want more of, so a network that