lement mechanisms, dashboards, and metrics that provide visibility into the Engineering department’s overall productivity, efficiency, and operational health.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Executive Reporting: Partner closely with the CTO and Chief of Staff to synthesise data and streamline company-wide reporting activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Facilitate Executive &amp; Client Engagements: Prepare high-quality briefings, presentations, and strategic materials for key executive meetings and client engagements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as an Organizational Connector: Bridge communication gaps between teams, remove critical bottlenecks, and rally resources to accelerate project timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a Tactical Force Multiplier: Step in where needed to fill gaps or unblock progress.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven Adaptability &amp; Execution: A track record of success in high-growth, fast-paced environments where agility, rapid delivery, and hands-on execution are critical.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert Programme Management: Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage a high volume of diverse projects, juggle competing priorities, and keep cross-functional teams tightly aligned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic Problem Solving: Experience bringing structure to highly ambiguous problems and successfully managing complex stakeholder relationships across the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-Impact Background: Prior experience navigating fluid, fast-moving environments, such as top-tier consulting firms, major business/technical transformation programs, or a previous role within a CTO Office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Literacy &amp; Fluency: Strong technical aptitude with a s