oals and improve their practices, supporting their growth and our retention goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI fluency in your team: coach engineers to use AI tools well, share what works, and make AI-assisted development part of how they grow.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><br /><strong>Tech</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive projects end to end, applying best-in-class engineering practices: clean architecture, strong test coverage, code review and observability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the adoption of AI across the development lifecycle, from coding agents and AI-assisted reviews to test generation and automated workflows. Set clear guardrails for quality, security and privacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in sprint delivery, monitor engineering metrics, and be accountable for the quality of what ships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring forward innovative solutions and encourage innovative thinking from others, including new ways AI can remove toil and speed up delivery.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br /><br />Delivery &amp; Impact</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Delivery Managers, Product Owners and Designers to assess feasibility, give technical recommendations, and help with estimation and planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focus the team on outcomes, not output: tie work to user and business impact, and measure it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delegate effectively so work is completed as specified, without micromanaging.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set clear expectations and make sure practices are followed to meet Ledger’s quality bar.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br /><br />Leadership &amp; Communication</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring a po