<p data-lfile-container="61d171d5-b814-4e82-b6c7-fbf6810c9455" data-pm-slice="1 1 []"><strong>Paris (Office-first)</strong></p>
<h3 id="team-description-1"><strong>Team description</strong></h3>
<p>SumUp already powers over 4 million businesses worldwide. We're now aiming for bigger names, and we're building the team to do it. In France, our Key Account Sales team goes after larger businesses, from hospitality groups to beauty chains and major retailers. You'll choose how you prospect, by phone or in the field, get into their networks and close the deals. As one of the first people on this new team, you'll help work out what it takes to win these accounts, with plenty of opportunities opening up as we grow. The best part? Your variable pay is uncapped, so there's no ceiling on what you can earn.</p>
<h3 id="what-youll-do-1"><strong>What you'll do</strong></h3>
<p>Identify and reach high-potential businesses, such as hospitality groups, beauty chains and major retailers</p>
<p>Run high-volume outreach by phone, in the field and through other channels</p>
<p>Get in front of decision-makers and understand how their business and sites operate</p>
<p>Book meetings and run tailored pitches and demos that show how SumUp can support their business</p>
<p>Own the full sales cycle, from first contact through to closing the deal</p>
<p>Grow your portfolio and network over time, using each win to open the next door</p>
<p>Track your performance against targets and use feedback and data to keep improving</p>
<h3 id="what-were-looking-for-1"><strong>What we're looking for…</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Proven experience in outbound sales, with a track record of hitting targets</li>
<li>Comfort with high volumes of outreach, by phone or in the field</li>
<li>Real drive and resilience: you stay motivated when deals take time or doors stay closed</li>
<li>Confidence and the ability to build strong relationships with business owners and decision-makers</li>
<li>Comfort with having freedom in how you work, alongside hands-on coaching and support from your team lead</li>
<li>Fluency in French and English</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="why-you-should-join-sumup-1"><strong>Why you should join SumUp</strong></h3>
<p>💰 Uncapped variable pay: strong performance can significantly increase your earnings</p>
<p>🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our Paris location. This involves an office-first setup</p>
<p>🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone's perspectives are respected and embraced</p>
<p>📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;D budget of €2,000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education</p>
<p>💼 Financial security: corporate pension contributions that support your long-term future</p>
<p>🏥 Healthcare support: we cover 50% of the monthly cost of your health insurance for your Mutuelle and Prévoyance</p>
<p>🚌 Extra allowances: we offer restaurant tickets (Swile) and cover transportation costs</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h2><strong>About SumUp</strong></h2>
<p>Be empowered to do more that matters.</p>
<p>At SumUp, we're on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 37 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.</p>
<p>Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI" target="_blank">our diverse team</a> of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/" target="_blank">Our core values</a> lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.</p>
<p>SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don't make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.sumup.com/careers/" target="_blank">careers website</a>, and follow our journey on <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>, <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/" target="_blank">Instagram</a>, and <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup" target="_blank">TikTok</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p><div class="content-conclusion"><p><strong>Job Application Tip</strong></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don't tick every box, it's ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.</span></p></div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/sumup/key-account-sales-executive-paris-173927","tags":[],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1794613527},{"slug":"remote-senior-growth-product-manager-paris-473086","company_name":"Soda Data Nv","title":"Senior Growth Product Manager","description":"<p>Data quality is the bottleneck of the AI era. Every Fortune 500 is trying to solve it. We're the team they call.</p><p>Soda is the data quality layer for Disney, Ralph Lauren, CBRE, HelloFresh, 2K Games, and Nubank. Our open-source engine, Soda Core, is used by companies like Tesla, Slack, Adyen, Walmart, and JPMC. The category is growing fast because AI doesn't work on bad data, and we're hiring a <strong>Senior Growth Product Manager</strong> to get customers using Soda faster and on more of their data.</p><h3>About Us</h3><p>Soda's mission is to monitor the world's decisions. We're building the first Data &amp; AI performance monitoring platform that spans data collection to automated decision-making. Soda helps customers find, understand, and fix data quality issues by combining automated post-production monitoring with pre-production pipeline data testing.</p><p>Soda was founded in 2019 by Maarten (employee #5 at Collibra) and Tom (creator of multiple open-source projects generating hundreds of millions in value). We commercialize through Soda Cloud and we're well-funded, with investors like Point 9 Capital, Hummingbird, Singular, and Eurazeo.</p><h3>The Role</h3><p>You'll lead our adoption team, a small group of frontend, full-stack, and AI engineers. The team works on onboarding and activation, on keeping workflows coherent across the product, on customer-facing dashboards, and on AI features that save users work.</p><p>Most of our roadmap is driven by what customers and prospects ask for. This team's work is driven by adoption metrics, because customers rarely ask for the things that would make them use Soda more. You'll start from a hypothesis, for example that changing a flow will get 20% more data contracts created, ship the change, and check whether it worked.</p><p>We sell to enterprises, so sample sizes are small and A/B tests rarely reach significance. You'll use product analytics, session replays, and conversations with users, and you'll often have to decide with incomplete data. This is a product role. If most of your growth experience is in paid acquisition or lifecycle email, it's probably the wrong fit. You'll also work closely with our Growth team, which is led by a co-founder, on launches and messaging.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul><li>Own the adoption metrics for Soda Cloud: time to first verified contract for new accounts, data coverage (datasets with contracts and monitors), weekly active datasets and users, and usage of AI features. You'll define them, make sure we can measure them, and improve them.</li><li>Own the UX of workflows across the product and keep them coherent for our two kinds of users: data engineers, and business users such as data stewards and governance leads.</li><li>Find where customers get stuck between signing the contract and running Soda on most of their data, and decide what to fix first.</li><li>Design and ship onboarding flows that get a new team to first value within days, including self-serve paths for technical teams that want to evaluate Soda on their own.</li><li>Put AI to work on adoption: decide which steps an agent should do for the user, ship them with the team, and measure whether people keep using them.</li><li>Work with Growth on launches and product marketing, and with our customer engineers on whatever is blocking rollouts at customers.</li></ul><h3>Hiring Process</h3><ol><li>Application: your CV, plus a short answer about one metric you moved (what it was, what you shipped, what happened, and what didn't work)</li><li>15-minute phone screen</li><li>First interview (60 min): a deep dive into product growth work you've done. Part of it is showing us something you shipped that you'd still be proud to demo.</li><li>Second interview (60 min): a working session on a real Soda adoption problem</li><li>Culture fit (45 min)</li></ol><p>We answer every application, and every candidate hears back within 3–5 days of each step. If it's not a hell yes, it's a no, and we'll tell you quickly and kindly.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h3>You Should Have</h3><ul><li><strong>5+ years in product, including at least 2 owning growth, activation, onboarding, or adoption in B2B SaaS</strong>: you were accountable for a metric for long enough to see whether your changes worked. In your application, tell us which metric it was, where it started and where it ended, what you shipped, and what didn't work.</li><li><strong>Product craft and taste</strong>: you love software and have used a lot of it yourself, so you know what a good product feels like. You keep scope small, work in short cycles with engineers and designers, run your own customer calls, and have well-reasoned opinions about UX.</li><li><strong>An AI-native way of working and building</strong>: you've shipped an AI-powered feature and measured whether people use it, you prototype with coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, etc.), and you're happy to open a small PR yourself for something like a copy change.</li><li><strong>You do your own analysis</strong>: you write SQL, build funnels yourself, and know when a sample is too small to conclude anything.</li><li><strong>Experience with technical products</strong>: you've built for engineers or data teams and are comfortable talking about pipelines, warehouses, and APIs.</li><li><strong>Clear writing and comfort working async</strong>: we're a distributed team across 12+ countries, and most decisions happen in writing, in English.</li></ul><p>The five years don't all have to be in a PM role. If you were a product engineer or a founder and owned a growth metric, please apply.</p><h3>Good to Have</h3><ul><li>Data quality, data observability, data governance, or data infrastructure experience.</li><li>Experience with product-led growth at a company that also sells to enterprises.</li><li>Experience with Shape Up or another fixed-time, variable-scope way of working.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul><li>Compensation €120,000–140,000/year + equity.</li><li>Outside Belgium, this is a contractor position.</li><li>Fully remote (EU-based), with a Belgian office available if you want one.</li><li>In-person kickoffs every two months in cool locations across Europe, three days with the whole product and engineering team.</li><li>All the tokens you need, across all frontier models.</li><li>Real ownership, real impact, no micromanagement.</li><li>A senior team that ships, across 12+ countries.</li></ul><h3>Our Values</h3><p>We value freedom with responsibility, transparency, and a growth mindset. We avoid politics, have no tolerance for dishonesty, and value open and direct communication without judgment. We proactively bring up and address potential issues before they become critical, and we overcommunicate frequently. Working at Soda, you will have full autonomy to make impactful product and roadmap decisions.</p><h3>❤️ Why you will love to join Soda</h3><ul><li><strong>You own the adoption metrics</strong>: you decide how we measure adoption and what we do to improve it.</li><li><strong>Lots of room to improve</strong>: we already have enterprise customers and usage data, and we've done very little growth work so far.</li><li><strong>Your own engineering team</strong>: you'll work with dedicated engineers who build agentically, so your ideas get shipped quickly.</li><li><strong>Be part of a transformation</strong>: data quality is having its moment, and we're at the front of it.</li><li><strong>Work on your own terms</strong>: fully remote, flexible hours, colleagues in 12+ countries.</li></ul><h3>😡 What you might not love</h3><ul><li><strong>Rapidly changing priorities</strong>: our roadmap can pivot quickly. It's a fast-paced environment with a LOT of work to be done.</li><li><strong>Small numbers</strong>: we have relatively few accounts and feedback is slow. If you're used to deciding from consumer-scale data, you may find that frustrating.</li><li><strong>No playbook</strong>: this is the first dedicated growth PM role at Soda.</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/soda-data-nv/remote-senior-growth-product-manager-paris-473086","tags":["Computer Software","Product and Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1794612009},{"slug":"sales-development-representative-zurich-209019","company_name":"Benchling","title":"Sales Development Representative","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are rebuilding biotech for the AI era.<br /><br />When a breakthrough is delayed, the world waits. Getting a molecule from discovery to patients, or a crop from lab to field, involves thousands of slow, manual, disconnected steps. AI has the potential to change this, compressing decades of R&amp;D work into years. But that only happens when clean, structured scientific data and AI are built into how science gets done.<br /><br />Benchling is the AI platform for biotech R&amp;D. Scientists use Benchling to design experiments, capture structured data, and run AI agents and models directly in their workflows. Over 200,000 scientists around the world trust Benchling to power their most important work, from academic labs to Sanofi, Moderna, and more than half of the world's top 50 biopharma.<br /><br />We’re building an AI scientist for our customers. We can’t do that if we haven’t built the muscle ourselves. AI fluency is the foundation we build on; it's core to how we work, and we're committed to helping every new hire integrate it into their day-to-day. As part of our interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>ROLE OVERVIEW</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a passionate and motivated Sales Development Representative with a love for selling and a tenacious and methodical approach to prospecting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a fantastic first impression with prospects and customers while building pipeline for Account Executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow up and qualify inbound requests and MQLs, via the telephone and email, for scientific fit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organize, categorize, and prioritize sales leads in Salesforce and measure lead conversion and performance against quota.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage prospecting tools to research companies and identify key decision makers at new accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop customized pitches for different target accounts and personas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Account Executives to drive outbound prospecting activities, including cold calling, emailing, and communicating our value proposition to decision makers.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the field marketing and sales teams to drive attendance at Benchling field events such as executive dinners and happy hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Staff tradeshows and follow-up on leads collected at the Benchling booth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Undergraduate degree in life sciences required (e.g. molecular biology, biotechnology, biomedical engineering, biochemistry), Postgraduate welcomed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recent graduate or 1-2 years of internship / work experience in a Sales Development Representative, Business Development Representative function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passionate about Benchling’s mission and the acceleration of life sciences research</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not afraid to pick up the phone and cold call in German</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong verbal and written communication skills in German and English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Persistent, self-motivated, and willing to go beyond strict job responsibilities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driven to meet/exceed goals with a proven history of consistent high achievement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gritty and resourceful</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Methodical and disciplined work ethic</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language Requirements: English AND German</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>HOW WE WORK</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a flexible hybrid work arrangement that prioritizes in-office collaboration. Employees are expected to be on-site 3 days per week (Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Hybrid #LI-Remote</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#BI-Hybrid #BI-Remote</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benchling welcomes everyone.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe diversity enriches our team so we hire people with a wide range of identities, backgrounds, and experiences. <br /><br />We are an equal opportunity employer. That means we don’t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including but not limited to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/benchling/sales-development-representative-zurich-209019","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich, Switzerland","created_at":1794638433},{"slug":"cell-culture-engineer-lausanne-297895","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Cell Culture Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're expanding our protein expression into mammalian cell culture, for example in CHO and HEK cells. Our mammalian expression volume is growing fast. We're looking for a Cell Culture Engineer who has spent years growing and transfecting mammalian cells and knows what to do when a run goes wrong.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work alongside our production and mammalian cell teams as a hands-on expert in the cell culture lab. You'll keep cultures healthy and on schedule, run transfections and expressions, and be the person the team turns to when yields drop or cells misbehave. This is a hands-on role, not a management role.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run mammalian expression.</strong> Maintain, expand, and passage cell lines, and run transfections and expressions on a production schedule.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Troubleshoot.</strong> When viability, growth, or yield falls off, find the cause and fix it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the cell bank.</strong> Thaw, freeze, and track cell stocks, and protect the lines from contamination and drift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optimize conditions.</strong> Test culture and transfection conditions, and turn what works into the standard protocol.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale with automation.</strong> Work with our automation team to move cell handling onto liquid handlers as volume grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hand off clean material.</strong> Deliver harvests ready for purification and downstream assays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep the lab running.</strong> Look after incubators, biosafety cabinets, and cell counters, and keep the BSL-2 space organized and compliant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Write SOPs and train.</strong> Document protocols that others can follow, and train the team on aseptic technique and our cell culture workflows.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive hands-on experience with common mammalian model cell lines, for example CHO and HEK, including transfection and expression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BSc / MSc in biotechnology, cell biology, or a relevant field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A troubleshooting track record. You've rescued failing cultures and expressions and can explain what went wrong and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flawless aseptic technique and experience working under BSL-2 conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high-throughput formats: multi-well plates and many conditions in parallel, not only flasks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with liquid handlers is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with antibody or Fc-fusion production is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organized and precise. You track every stock, passage, and transfection, and you follow protocols exactly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI tools effectively and with discernment. We use them across the company and expect you to check, edit, and stand behind what they produce, not pass along unreviewed output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in a fast-paced environment where priorities shift. Cells don't keep office hours, so you plan around them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/cell-culture-engineer-lausanne-297895","tags":["Biology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1794638431},{"slug":"startup-operations-generalist-lausanne-148919","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Startup Operations Generalist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are growing fast and opening a second lab in London. Every new person, contract, invoice and payroll run lands on someone's desk. You own that desk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the operations generalist seat: finance admin, payroll, people operations, hiring logistics, and whatever else the company needs to run well. You own the machinery so that everyone else spends their time on the lab.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a strategy role and not a pure HR role. It is hands-on, and most of the work is making sure things happen correctly and on time, then making sure they happen without you next time.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run payroll and people admin.</strong> Monthly payroll and the relationship with our payroll provider, contracts, onboarding and offboarding, benefits and pension, leave and absence. Every person gets paid correctly and every new hire has a laptop, accounts and a contract on day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run the finance back office.</strong> Supplier invoices and payment runs, customer invoicing and collections, expense and card reconciliation, and the monthly hand-off to our external accountants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep hiring moving.</strong> Interview scheduling, candidate logistics, NDAs, work-trial setup and offer paperwork in Ashby. You make sure the hiring process never stalls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep us compliant.</strong> Swiss and UK employment rules, permits and visas, insurance, VAT filings, company registers. You are not a lawyer or an accountant, but you know when to call one and you make sure deadlines never surprise us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own general operations.</strong> Office and lab-site logistics, vendor and software contracts, renewals, company-wide tools and access. When something is nobody's job, it is yours until it has an owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate all of the above.</strong> Payroll, invoicing, our ATS and our ledger all have APIs. The goal is that each process you take over runs with less manual work every quarter.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You have run operations at a fast-growing startup.</strong> Several years covering some mix of finance admin, payroll, HR and office operations, ideally as the first or second person doing it. You have built processes, not only followed them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Detail-obsessed.</strong> A wrong payslip or a missed filing is a real problem for a real person. You check the numbers before anyone asks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-native.</strong> It's 2026. We run on Claude Code across the company, and you use AI tools and scripts to automate your own work. You check what they produce and stand behind the result. The more software engineering experience you have, the better. If your instinct is that operations is a spreadsheet-and-inbox job, we will frustrate each other.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Swiss or UK employment and payroll experience is a plus.</strong> Social charges, pension, permits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Self-starter.</strong> Nobody hands you a prioritized queue. You see what is broken or about to break, and you fix it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trustworthy with everything.</strong> Salaries, contracts, personal data and company finances all cross your desk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English required.</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/startup-operations-generalist-lausanne-148919","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1794638431},{"slug":"scientific-account-manager-ai-biotech-lausanne-140471","company_name":"Adaptyv","title":"Scientific Account Manager, AI & Biotech","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptyv is building an automated lab that lets AI agents run biology experiments. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're entering the era of agentic science where AI models can now design novel proteins, propose hypotheses, and iterate on experimental results. But they can't run the experiments themselves - that's still a manual, months-long process. We're building the infrastructure that gives AI agents access to the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing biotech companies, trusted by leading biopharmas, frontier AI labs, and the techbio companies pushing the field forward. This is a rare chance to help advance some of the most important work happening in biotech today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our automated lab is powered by a deep software + hardware stack: lab instruments worth millions of USD reverse-engineered into API-controllable hardware, dozens of devices orchestrated through complex workflows, full observability on everything that happens in the lab, processing pipelines for messy physical-world data, and AI systems that troubleshoot production results and accelerate assay development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing rapidly and are hiring for talented people to scale and support the massive demand for AI-driven wet lab experimentation.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers are AI labs and biotechs that design biology. They send us their designs, our automated lab runs the experiments, and they get the data back. The first experiment is only the start. We want every customer to run their next experiment with us, and the one after that.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own a portfolio of AI-lab and biotech accounts after the first deal is signed. You make sure each project lands. You learn where each customer's research is going, and you turn that into the next order.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run your accounts.</strong> You are the main contact for your customers, from project kickoff to delivery of results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep projects on track.</strong> You work with the lab and our forward-deployed scientists, so timelines hold and customers always know where things stand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow revenue.</strong> You find the next experiment, the larger campaign, the new team inside the same company. Renewals and expansion are your number.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring the customer's voice back.</strong> You tell product and the lab what customers need next.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Account growth experience.</strong> You have managed and grown accounts in biotech, life-science tools or technical B2B. You have grown accounts, not only kept them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scientific fluency.</strong> An MSc or PhD in biochemistry, protein engineering or a related field. You can read binding kinetics and expression data, and discuss assay design and results with a protein designer as a peer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organized and reliable.</strong> You hold timelines, and no customer email sits unanswered.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Self-starter.</strong> Nobody hands you a playbook. You see what an account needs and do it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-native.</strong> It's 2026: you use Claude and similar tools every day to prepare, follow up and stay on top of your accounts, and you check what they produce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At home in AI x bio.</strong> You follow protein design models and the labs that build them. A plus, not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application deadline</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are reviewing applicants on a rolling basis.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/adaptyv/scientific-account-manager-ai-biotech-lausanne-140471","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1794638431},{"slug":"senior-business-analyst-syrius-uvg-zurich-98656","company_name":"QuBit Consulting & Solutions AG","title":"Senior Business Analyst - Syrius / UVG","description":"<p>Für ein anspruchsvolles Projekt im Schweizer Versicherungsumfeld suchen wir einen erfahrenen <strong>Senior Business Analyst mit fundierten Kenntnissen in der Unfallversicherung (UVG)</strong>. Im Fokus stehen zunächst die <strong>fachliche Vorbereitung, Konzeption und Aufgleisung eines grösseren Implementierungsprojekts</strong>. Im Anschluss besteht die Möglichkeit einer Verlängerung zur fachlichen Begleitung der Umsetzung.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h2>Tasks</h2><ul><li><p>Analyse und Strukturierung bestehender Geschäftsprozesse im Bereich UVG</p></li><li><p>Fachliche Vorbereitung und Aufgleisung des Implementierungsprojekts inklusive Scope, Anforderungen und Umsetzungsplanung auf Basis von Syrius / UVG</p></li><li><p>Erarbeitung von Fachkonzepten und Definition der zukünftigen fachlichen Architektur</p></li><li><p>Gestaltung und Optimierung der zukünftigen Geschäftsprozesse und Systemlandschaft<