bzw. Kreditportfoliomanagement auch aus methodischer Sicht / Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse.</p><p>Ihr Kontakt:</p><p>Herr Ivano Coni ist gerne für Sie da. Ihre Bewerbung wird streng vertraulich behandelt.</p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/senior-analyst-risk-control-lombard-kredite-zurich-366724","tags":["Credit Analysis"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794632424},{"slug":"financial-mathematician-cross-assets-asset-management-zurich-358312","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Financial Mathematician Cross Assets | Asset Management","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarter in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is the asset management of an international bank in Zurich. We are looking for a quantitative finance specialist (m, f, d) as a</p><p><strong>Financial Mathematician Cross Assets | Asset Management</strong></p><p>Your Tasks:</p><p>Risk- and performance-oriented quantitative analysis and calculations for a wide range of asset classes including fund investments in the field of the bank's asset management / Foster in-depth risk analyses, estimates and recommendations based on high quality assessments using e.g. Bloomberg, Morningstar, RiskMetrix, etc. /  Monitoring of risk positions in the investment portfolios / Preparation of reports containing risk analytics and key performance indicators for internal and external stakeholders / Refine methodologies to constantly expand the analysis and reporting capabilities / Optimizing asset management strategies, products, processes and tools / Work closely with other team members, portfolio managers and senior management / Regular reporting to the Head of Asset Management / Participation in projects focused on the continuous development of infrastructure, tools and methods.</p><p>Your Profile:</p><p>Master in Finance or Quantitative Finance / Professional experience in asset management at a bank or a major fund manager, or in fund auditing / Experience in risk & performance calculation across equity, fixed income, multi-asset and fund portfolios, including private equity Investments / Experience with a broad range of  portfolio calculations e.g. portfolio risk calculations, sensitivity analysis, factor exposures, concentration limits, liquidity risk, tracking error, etc. / Experience with investment restriction set up and controlling / Extensive experience with Bloomberg, Morningstar, RiskMetrix, etc. essential / Programming skills: SQL, VBA and Python, etc., for the further development of various in-house tools / Strong analytical skills / Team-oriented with process oriented thinking and problem solving mentality / Ability to go into details and to communicate the results to internal stakeholders and investors.</p><p>Your Contact:</p><p>Mr. Ivano Coni would like to support you. Your application will be kept strictly confidential.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>8032 ----- </p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/financial-mathematician-cross-assets-asset-management-zurich-358312","tags":["Asset","Fonds Management"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794630658},{"slug":"senior-data-architect-senior-data-engineer-azure-databricks-39403","company_name":"Xebiadach","title":"Senior Data Architect / Senior Data Engineer – Azure Databricks","description":"&lt;p&gt;Remote, occasionally Zurich · 80–100% · Start as soon as possible ·&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Xebia&lt;/strong&gt; pushes the boundaries of what’s possible – and you’re right in the middle of it! We’re not just consultants, but visionaries: with more than 5,000 experts worldwide, we help our clients drive their digital transformation with passion and ambition. At Xebia, it’s about more than recommendations: with innovative solutions, we create a unique combination of technology, people and processes. Our goal is to make our clients digital frontrunners – ready to turn media usage data into insights that make a difference?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the project&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our client, a large Swiss media company, is building a new platform on Azure Databricks for the usage data of its apps and websites. It will replace the commercial analytics tool they use today. Analysts are starting to work on the new platform now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You join the platform team of five developers through Xebia. Most of your time goes into implementing Jira tickets. You build and run the pipelines that take event data from Azure Event Hubs through the bronze, silver and gold layers into the tables analysts and dashboards use. You keep the Databricks and Azure infrastructure in code with Pulumi and ship changes through GitHub Actions. The team creates and refines tickets together and reviews each other&#39;s code. You&#39;ll also help analysts get started with Databricks and GitHub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the senior person in the team, you can advise on anything from implementation details to the overall architecture, while the product owner sets the priorities. Today the role also covers the data model, the infrastructure and the platform costs, and there is room to take on more responsibility over time. The team uses AI coding assistants such as Claude in its daily work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Several years of hands-on data engineering on Databricks: building and running production pipelines with Spark, PySpark or SQL and Delta Lake, in a medallion architecture&lt;br&gt;• Architecture experience on a Databricks or Azure data platform&lt;br&gt;• Streaming or event ingestion, ideally Azure Event Hubs or Kafka&lt;br&gt;• Data modelling for analytics and BI&lt;br&gt;• Infrastructure as code, ideally Pulumi (Terraform experience transfers)&lt;br&gt;• Git, GitHub workflows and CI/CD with GitHub Actions&lt;br&gt;• Experience in larger projects&lt;br&gt;• You work well in a team and get productive with little onboarding&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable using AI coding assistants&lt;br&gt;• Fluent English&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Unity Catalog, Databricks Asset Bundles, data quality frameworks&lt;br&gt;• Dashboards in Databricks or Power BI&lt;br&gt;• Azure experience beyond Databricks&lt;br&gt;• Web and app usage tracking or digital analytics, including tracking migrations&lt;br&gt;• Media or broadcasting experience&lt;br&gt;• German&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The current engineer can hand over until the end of January. English is the working language; German is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes us special&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;strong&gt;Innovation potential:&lt;/strong&gt; At Xebia, the focus is on innovation and pioneering spirit. You can develop your creative ideas and share innovative thoughts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌱 &lt;strong&gt;Personal growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We believe in personal development for outstanding professional experiences. Unlock your potential and keep growing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝 &lt;strong&gt;Community and networking:&lt;/strong&gt; Xebia is a community of technology enthusiasts. Meet professionals from different fields, share knowledge and shape innovation together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚖️ &lt;strong&gt;Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; We value work-life balance. Adapt your working hours and find a balance between your career and your personal life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;strong&gt;Great social events:&lt;/strong&gt; Ski days, B2run, spontaneous after-work apéros, Christmas and summer parties – we celebrate together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to take your professional journey further, we warmly welcome you to Xebia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We look forward to meeting you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/xebiadach/senior-data-architect-senior-data-engineer-azure-databricks-39403","tags":["Delivery"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794628526},{"slug":"head-of-product-zurich-263883","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Head of Product","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our engineering teams build a product that enterprises run their purchase-to-pay and order-to-cash processes on every day. Much of the product knowledge behind it sits with our founders and domain experts. As we grow, we are moving from a project-oriented model, where features come top-down and success is measured by output, to a product-oriented one: empowered teams that own problems end-to-end and are measured by their impact on customers and the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Head of Product, you lead that shift. You build the product management practice for the BLP Platform from an early stage. Our first product managers are joining stream-aligned teams, starting with Invoice and Procurement, and the team will grow to 4–5 PMs as we expand. You hire them, coach them, and set the standard for what great product work looks like at BLP.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You report to the CTO and work closely with Engineering, Projects, Sales, and our founders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the product management practice for the BLP Platform: hire, coach, and develop a team of product managers as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Move the product organization from an output-driven model to an outcome-driven one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish the product management craft at BLP: discovery practices, evidence-based decision making, and a clear standard for what “good” looks like in the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transfer product knowledge out of the experts’ heads and into the teams, without losing the domain depth that got us here.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the direct line between our teams and our customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make our data usable for product decisions. We have BigQuery, PostHog, and prediction-rate analytics available, and we want product managers who reach for them by default.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how the product organization works as we grow: intake, prioritization, roadmapping, and the operating rhythm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute directly to product strategy for the platform.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years in product management, including experience leading or formally coaching product managers, with a real point of view on how product people are developed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in an empowered product model, where teams were assigned problems to solve rather than features to build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of shipping enterprise B2B software that customers actually adopted.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience moving an organization toward an empowered product model, including the political and cultural side of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to hold a position with engineers, sales, and executives, and to say no in a way that keeps the relationship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial judgment: comfortable operating with incomplete information, choosing a direction, and owning the result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enterprise ERP or finance exposure, experience with AI or agentic products in production (particularly reliability, evaluation, and trust in enterprise settings), and German are a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a function: you shape how product management works at BLP while the team grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct work with the CTO and founders on product strategy for the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product with deep domain substance and a large enterprise customer base to learn from.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee participation plan.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> We create measurable business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency:</strong> We build trust through openness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> We take responsibility for outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence:</strong> We relentlessly strive for greatness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Practical information</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: hybrid from our Zurich, London, Munich or Cologne offices, or remote elsewhere in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employment: full-time, permanent.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/head-of-product-zurich-263883","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1794627628},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-zurich-374197","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Senior Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product decisions for your team's area of the blp platform: what gets built, in what order, and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The outcomes your team is accountable for, not the output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discovery: understanding the users and customers in your area deeply enough that you can make most decisions yourself, and knowing which decisions need evidence first.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you shape with us</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product strategy for your area, in partnership with product leadership and the domain experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">How the product organization works as it scales: intake, prioritization, and the operating rhythm. We are actively iterating these, and we want the people doing the work to shape them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The standard for product management at blp, which is still being set.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you work with</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your stream-aligned team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Other SATs and the platform teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customers and key users directly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founders and domain experts, who hold a lot of the accumulated product knowledge in this space.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll bring</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of shipping enterprise B2B software that customers actually adopted.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial judgment. Comfortable operating with incomplete information, choosing a direction, and owning the result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experienced in product discovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can hold a position with engineers, with sales, and with executives, and can say no in a way that keeps the relationship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strongly preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in an empowered product model, where teams were assigned problems to solve rather than features to build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A plus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enterprise ERP or finance exposure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI or agentic products in production, particularly reliability, evaluation, and trust in enterprise settings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German, given our customer base.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership.</strong> What gets built in your area is yours, from strategy through outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A product org still taking shape.</strong> Real room to shape how it works, not just execute within it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct access.</strong> To founders, domain experts, and the customers you're building for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An empowered model.</strong> A seat in it, working with strong engineering and design partners.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about blp and our values at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://blp.digital/company/careers">blp.digital/company/careers</a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/senior-product-manager-zurich-374197","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1794627628},{"slug":"key-account-manager-german-speaking-territory-zurich-104815","company_name":"Justone Gr","title":"Key Account Manager (German Speaking Territory)","description":"<p>On behalf of our client, an international pharmaceutical company specializing in oncology, we are looking for an experienced and results-driven <strong>Key Account Manager</strong> to develop its business across German-speaking Switzerland.</p><p>We welcome candidates with a strong background in <strong>Oncology, Hematology, Immunology or other specialized therapeutic areas</strong>, particularly those with proven experience engaging directly with hospitals, private clinics and specialist physicians.</p><p>This is a field-based position (over 80% of time in the field), combining strategic account management, scientific engagement and commercial business development.</p><p></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Develop and execute territory sales strategies to achieve business objectives.</li><li>Build and maintain strong relationships with specialist physicians, oncologists, KOLs, hospital pharmacists and healthcare stakeholders.</li><li>Identify business opportunities and expand the company's presence within hospitals and private clinics.</li><li>Conduct high-quality scientific and product discussions with healthcare professionals.</li><li>Monitor market trends, competitor activities and customer needs.</li><li>Collaborate closely with Medical, Marketing and Market Access teams.</li><li>Organize and participate in scientific meetings, educational events and congresses.</li><li>Maintain accurate CRM reporting and ensure compliance with pharmaceutical regulations and pharmacovigilance requirements.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>University degree in Life Sciences, Business or a related field.</li><li><strong>Minimum 5 years of experience</strong> in pharmaceutical or biotech sales, preferably in Oncology, Hematology, Immunology or other specialty care areas.</li><li><strong>Proven experience working directly with hospitals, private clinics, specialist physicians and healthcare decision-makers.</strong></li><li>Strong understanding of the Swiss healthcare system and hospital environment.</li><li><strong>Fluent German (mandatory)</strong> and strong professional English; French is an advantage.</li><li>Excellent commercial, negotiation and relationship-building skills.</li><li>Autonomous, proactive, results-oriented and well-organized.</li><li>Proficiency in CRM tools and MS Office.</li><li>Valid Swiss driving licence (Category B).</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Annual Base Gross Salary: €110K/yr - €130K/yr </strong></li><li>Bonus </li><li>Private Health Insurance</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/justone-gr/key-account-manager-german-speaking-territory-zurich-104815","tags":["Sales","Pharmaceuticals"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794626403},{"slug":"senior-program-manager-el2-european-tour-olten-339868","company_name":"Electraaero","title":"Senior Program Manager, EL2 European Tour","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Electra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Air travel is about to become something more: more direct, more accessible, and more connected to the places where people live, work and want to be. Every day in the U.S., people make 35 million trips of 50–500 miles, stuck in traffic or routed through crowded hubs. Chances are, you&#39;ve been one of them. At Electra, we&#39;re changing that with the EL9, a nine-passenger, hybrid-electric aircraft that takes off and lands in just 150 feet. Our Ultra Short technology opens up thousands of new places to fly, beyond conventional runways, congested airports and long drives. We&#39;re backed by Lockheed Martin, Honeywell and Safran. Operators worldwide have signed intent-to-purchase agreements for the first 2,200 aircraft we produce, and we&#39;re moving toward first test flights in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Getting a new kind of aircraft airborne takes more than ambition. It takes our kind of bold: people who think big while working in the real world. Who move ideas into action and collaborate without silos. Who put people first and make room at the table for everyone. Who challenge one another without diminishing one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Sound like you? Then look beyond what you thought were your own limits, and help us take flight beyond runways.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Electra seeks an experienced Program Manager to lead the planning and execution of a European tour for Electra&#39;s EL2 technology demonstrator aircraft. This role will serve as the primary team lead for the EL2 program, partnering closely with engineering, flight test, government and commercial stakeholders, and company leadership to ensure the tour achieves its strategic objectives safely, on schedule, and within budget. &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;After the completion of the European tour this role will transition to supporting EL9. &amp;nbsp;The exact nature of this support will depend on the candidates specific skills and interest areas; likely options include test team program management, program office support, or leading teams executing government contract&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tour Planning and Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop a master schedule, budget, and resourcing plan for the tour, including aircraft transport/ferry logistics, ground support, and personnel deployment to meet the overall mission objectives and success critera.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate with Sales, Business Development, and Government Affairs to prioritization of target locations, stakeholders, and events (e.g., customer demonstrations, government engagements, airshows) across the tour itinerary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cross-Functional Coordination&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Flight Test and Engineering teams to ensure the aircraft, crew, and support equipment are mission-ready for each tour stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate with Legal, Regulatory, and International Trade/Export Control functions to secure necessary permissions, airspace access, and customs clearances for international operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Serve as the central point of coordination between internal teams and external partners, hosts, and government counterparts at each location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Manage vendor and logistics partners supporting ground operations, transport, and lodging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Risk Management and Execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify, track, and mitigate risks related to schedule, safety, logistics, weather, and geopolitical factors across tour locations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop contingency plans for schedule disruptions, maintenance needs, or changes in stop-level objectives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Monitor tour execution in real time and adjust plans as needed to maintain safety and achieve strategic goals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Maintain clear documentation and traceability of decisions, approvals, and changes throughout the tour&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Reporting and Communication&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Provide regular status updates to program and executive leadership on tour progress, risks, and outcomes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Capture and communicate lessons learned and stakeholder feedback from each tour stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Support internal and external communications/marketing efforts related to the tour&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Deliver a post-tour summary with key outcomes, metrics, and recommendations for future campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Business, or related field, or equivalent experience (advanced degree a plus)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;US Persons required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;8+ years in program or project management, ideally within aerospace, defense, or a related complex technical industry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Proven track record managing complex, multi-stakeholder programs with tight schedules and significant logistical coordination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience working with international operations, export control considerations, and cross-border logistics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Strong organizational and risk management skills, with the ability to adapt plans quickly in dynamic environments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cross-functionally with engineering, flight test, legal, and business teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, including experience engaging with government and/or customer audiences&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Willingness and ability to travel internationally, potentially for extended periods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience supporting flight test campaigns, demonstration tours, or airshow operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with European aviation regulatory environments and airspace coordination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience working with government or defense customers internationally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Prior experience with aircraft ferry/transport logistics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance; STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO, sick leave, and company holidays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Paid winter break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;401(k) with immediate vesting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free catered lunches, coffee, snacks, and drinks at our Manassas headquarters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free on-site parking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Electra is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position may be subject to ITAR requirements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/electraaero/senior-program-manager-el2-european-tour-olten-339868","tags":["Product Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"Olten","created_at":1794606956},{"slug":"director-customer-success-basel-399824","company_name":"Prudentia Sciences","title":"Director, Customer Success","description":"<h2><strong>About Prudentia Sciences</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prudentia Sciences is the scientific intelligence layer powering life sciences dealmaking. We bring together expert-developed scientific diligence frameworks, AI reasoning trained on drug development, and a unified evidence base to accelerate investment in breakthrough therapies. As a trusted third party operating between buyer and seller, we help build conviction through every stage of the deal, faster. We replace fragmented workflows with a single system that surfaces what matters earlier.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by GV (Google Ventures), McKesson, Iaso Ventures, Virtue, and SignalFire - and built by people who have sat on every side of the table in life sciences dealmaking - we're on a mission to bring expert scientific judgment to every deal decision, at AI scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a <strong>Director of Customer Success</strong> to manage and scale a portfolio of strategic biopharma accounts. You'll own commercial outcomes for Top 25 biopharma customers, driving platform adoption, retention, and expansion to build a “business within the business”. Customer feedback from your portfolio will directly inform our product roadmap and operating model. You’ll operate with the judgment of an owner, not just execute a playbook.</p><h2><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial strategy</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own a portfolio of strategic biopharma accounts; drive the full commercial lifecycle - from implementation and onboarding through to retention and partnership expansion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute account-level strategy, identifying expansion opportunities and leading renewal negotiations to achieve industry-leading retention rates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor usage patterns, engagement signals, and business outcomes to proactively grow accounts and manage partnership signals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transform satisfied customers into vocal advocates who provide references, case studies, testimonials, and speak at industry events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the voice of the customer to Product, Engineering, Sales, and Scientific teams, ensuring market feedback drives our product roadmap and strategic priorities</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead Implementation and Drive Adoption</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orchestrate complex customer implementations including platform configuration, custom development, and data integrations aligned to customer use cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and execute account-specific onboarding strategies, facilitating executive workshops, design sessions, and hands-on trainings that accelerate time-to-value</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively communicate product updates, new capabilities, and innovative use cases to maximize customer value realization</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide Expert Technical Support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diagnose and resolve platform issues through systematic troubleshooting, documenting problems clearly and coordinating with Engineering on appropriate resolution paths</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop deep platform expertise that enables you to answer complex technical questions and guide customers through sophisticated workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create feedback loops that ensure technical issues inform long-term product improvements</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of customer success, management consulting, partnerships, account management, or implementation experience in pharmaceutical, biopharma, biotech, or life sciences industries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of drug development processes, portfolio management, and deal evaluation frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to navigate complex, multi-stakeholder decision-making within large enterprise organizations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical aptitude, with the ability to quickly master sophisticated software platforms and translate technical capabilities into business value</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional executive communication skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial mindset with comfort operating in fast-paced, high-growth environments where priorities evolve quickly</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus points</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience in biopharma Search &amp; Evaluation, Business Development, Licensing, Portfolio Management, or Strategy roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of driving measurable customer outcomes, achieving retention and expansion targets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with AI/ML platforms, advanced analytics tools, or decision intelligence software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with customer success platforms (HubSpot, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced degree (MS, PhD, MBA) in life sciences, business, or a related field</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are strongly prioritizing candidates based in London (UK), Dublin (Ireland), or Basel (Switzerland) to support our EU-based clients. Today this role will be remote as we do not have a physical office in these locations, but as we scale, we intend to be hybrid 2x per week (Tues/Thurs).</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €89K – €110K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Dublin, Ireland • €89K – €110K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li><li>London, England • £85K – £110K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li><li>Basel, Switzerland • CHF 117K – CHF 150K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/prudentia-sciences/director-customer-success-basel-399824","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Basel, Switzerland","created_at":1794606017},{"slug":"science-manager-nature-based-solutions-80-100-zurich-11321","company_name":"Climeworks","title":"Science Manager – Nature-based Solutions (80-100%)","description":"<p><span style="color:#121317">As a Science Manager in Climeworks Solutions, you make sure that our nature-based solutions (NBS) portfolio meets the same demanding quality bar we apply to all our carbon dioxide removal offerings. Your focus is on Afforestation, Reforestation and Revegetation (ARR), Improved Forest Management (IFM) and Mangroves, but you are not limited to these. You will screen the market, identify and assess priority projects, and carry out due diligence on potential partners. You form and defend Climeworks Solutions' own, independent scientific view on the quality, risks and fit of NBS projects. You keep our assessment criteria up to date and apply them in practice. You work closely with the sourcing team to shape our approach to nature credits, from first supplier contact to partnerships and product positioning. This role gives you real influence on how we build our nature offering and how the wider removal market develops.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Quality framework development:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You adapt and sharpen Climeworks' quality assessment frameworks for nature-based pathways. You draw on the newest published methodologies and on standards as they evolve.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Supplier assessment and monitoring:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You build constructive relationships with relevant suppliers. You rate and benchmark their projects. Over time, you track how project quality and delivery change and flag any concerns early.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Project due diligence:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You run in-depth technical, scientific and commercial reviews of key projects. These cover additionality, 