T-Lösungen</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <ul><li><p>Abgeschlossene Ausbildung im Bereich Informatik, idealerweise mit Schwerpunkt Systemtechnik oder Plattformen &amp; Infrastruktur</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Mehrjährige Berufserfahrung als System Engineer in komplexen ICT-Umgebungen, vorzugsweise im IT-Service- oder Consulting-Umfeld</p></li><li><p>Fundierte Kenntnisse in Netzwerk-Technologien wie TCP/IP, Routing, Switching, VLAN und VPN</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung mit Firewall- und Security-Lösungen sowie modernen Infrastrukturplattformen</p></li><li><p>Gute Kenntnisse in Server-, Storage- und Virtualisierungsumgebungen</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung mit Microsoft-Technologien, insbesondere Microsoft 365 und Azure</p></li><li><p>Kenntnisse im Bereich VoIP und moderner Kommunikationslösungen von Vorteil</p></li><li><p>Analytische Denkweise und Freude daran, technische Herausforderungen nachhaltig zu lösen</p></li><li><p>Selbstständige, strukturierte und lösungsorientierte Arbeitsweise</p></li><li><p>Kommunikationsstärke sowie Freude an der Zusammenarbeit mit Kunden und Teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/system-engineer-cloud-network-security-steinhausen-30293","tags":["Infrastructure & DevOps"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Steinhausen, Zug, Switzerland","created_at":1794562296},{"slug":"dynamics-365-crm-solution-architect-zurich-82072","company_name":"SwissPeak Partners GmbH","title":"Dynamics 365 CRM Solution Architect","description":"<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer">Our client is an international IT consulting company with a strong focus on Microsoft technologies. As a Microsoft implementation partner, the company delivers CRM projects based on Microsoft Dynamics 365 for well known clients across various industries. It combines deep technical expertise with a strong consulting mindset.</p> <br> <ul><li><p>Take ownership of solution architecture and technical design for Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM implementations</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Gather and analyse customer requirements</p></li><li><p>Conduct fit gap analyses and translate business requirements into technical solutions</p></li><li><p>Design and document CRM architectures, including integration and data models</p></li><li><p>Provide technical leadership to implementation teams</p></li><li><p>Coordinate external partners and stakeholders</p></li><li><p>Advise customers at eye level, from strategic planning through to implementation</p></li><li><p>Ensure adherence to Microsoft best practices and architectural standards</p></li><li><p>Support pre sales activities and customer presentations</p></li><li><p>Mentor and support junior consultants</p></li></ul><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong><br>Your Profile</strong></p><ul><li><p>At least 5 years of experience in the Microsoft Dynamics 365 environment</p></li><li><p>Several years of experience in a solution architecture or senior consulting role</p></li><li><p>Strong practical knowledge of Dynamics 365 CE, Sales and Customer Service</p></li><li><p>Solid experience with Microsoft Power Platform and Dataverse</p></li><li><p>Experience designing integration architectures with Azure and third party systems</p></li><li><p>Previous consulting or project experience is an advantage</p></li><li><p>Very good German skills, minimum C1 level. Good command of English</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/dynamics-365-crm-solution-architect-zurich-82072","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Zurich, Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794562296},{"slug":"it-solution-architect-bern-227761","company_name":"SwissPeak Partners GmbH","title":"IT Solution Architect","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">Are you an IT architect who is equally comfortable designing a cloud architecture and getting hands-on to implement it? This might be for you.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">We are looking for an IT System Architect on behalf of our client, a leading Swiss manufacturing company based in Canton Bern. The company is on a clear cloud transformation journey and needs someone to own it, drive it, and make it happen.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">You will be responsible for designing, implementing, and evolving the company's Azure cloud architecture end-to-end. This means taking ownership of Landing Zone design, hybrid networking, Entra ID and identity management, Azure Governance and policy frameworks, and security architecture. Beyond Azure, you will also take a broader IT architecture responsibility: defining standards, evaluating new technologies, coordinating external partners, and ensuring the company's IT landscape evolves in a structured and sustainable way. You will act as the trusted technical advisor to IT leadership and be expected to build internal know-how over time.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>You know Azure deeply, from having built things hands-on.</p></li><li><p>You are structured enough to think architecturally and pragmatic enough to roll up your sleeves when needed</p></li><li><p>You have experience coordinating external vendors and partners and keeping delivery on track</p></li><li><p>You communicate clearly with both engineers and management</p></li><li><p>You speak German fluently</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Role info</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>Permanent position, 100% workload, Bern</p></li><li><p>Flexibility on remote work discussed at interview stage</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Interested? Apply directly to learn more!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/it-solution-architect-bern-227761","tags":["Infrastructure & DevOps"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Bern, Berne, Switzerland","created_at":1794562296},{"slug":"sr-engineering-manager-developer-ecosystem-amsterdam-300494","company_name":"databricks","title":"Sr. Engineering Manager - Developer Ecosystem","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;RDQ427R369&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about enabling data teams to solve the world&#39;s toughest problems — from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world&#39;s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Developer Ecosystem organisation shapes how developers and the AI agents working for them build on the Databricks Data and AI Platform, from within the product to the tools they already use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring an Engineering Manager to lead our declarative deployment framework, which turns data and AI projects into versioned, reviewable, repeatable software. It is one product with two entry points. Third-party developers use our open-source CLI from their IDEs, terminals, and CI/CD systems. First-party, they author, deploy and inspect the same projects inside the Databricks workspace. In both, AI agents increasingly do the work: coding agents drive the CLI, and our in-product AI assistant authors and deploys projects alongside the developer. Thousands of organisations run their CI/CD on it, and it is one of the fastest-growing parts of the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team owns the deployment engine and CLI, the in-workspace authoring and deployment experience, and the metadata service and deployment history that record every deployment. The hard problems are real infrastructure-as-code problems: reconciling declared and live state, making plans safe for humans and agents to approve, keeping visual authoring and code in sync, and shipping weekly releases that remain backwards-compatible for our largest customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and grow the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage a team of senior engineers across three closely connected areas (the deployment engine and open-source CLI, the in-workspace authoring and deployment experience, and deployment history and metadata), working with strong tech leads. Hire, coach and promote, and grow engineers into tech leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make agentic development the default path:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape how developers and AI agents author, validate and deploy projects, both inside the workspace and from the developer&#39;s own coding agent. Design the tools, skills and guardrails so agents get the same safety and auditability as humans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Product and Design to set a multi-quarter roadmap for declarative deployment: agentic development, governed deployments and deployment history, enterprise CI/CD, and new resource coverage. Make the trade-offs explicit when the demand is larger than the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar on execution and operational excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Run a predictable delivery process for a fast-moving, open-source product with frequent releases. Own reliability, on-call health, incident response and the quality bar for a tool customers depend on to ship to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treat backward compatibility as a product feature:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead engine and configuration migrations without forcing customers through a flag day, and communicate change clearly to customers, the community and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead across the platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive alignment with the many platform teams whose resources and services the framework deploys, and with our sibling teams in Developer Ecosystem (SDKs, CLI, IaC provider, IDE). Make the whole toolchain feel like one product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years managing software engineering teams, and 8+ years of software engineering experience overall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and shipping developer tools or platforms used by many external developers or internal teams, such as infrastructure-as-code, deployment or CI/CD systems, CLIs, SDKs, or internal developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of declarative systems and deployment workflows: plan/apply, state management, drift and reconciliation, environment promotion, GitOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical depth to engage on architecture and trade-offs with senior and staff engineers, and to hold a high-quality bar for public, versioned interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams through ambiguity, with competing priorities from customers, partners and platform dependencies, and making clear calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and a customer-first mindset. You enjoy talking to developers, reading their issues, and turning feedback into roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, including with executives, partner teams and an external developer community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stand-out experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or led teams on infrastructure-as-code or deployment platforms, e.g. Terraform, Pulumi, AWS CDK / CloudFormation, Kubernetes controllers, Argo CD / Flux / Helm, or Vercel / Netlify-style deploy platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed an open-source developer tool with an active community and a frequent release cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped developer workflows for AI coding agents (CLI-first tooling, agent skills, MCP), or AI-assisted authoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have managed managers or multiple teams (~15 to 20+ engineers), owned a multi-year platform strategy, and grown tech leads and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/databricks/sr-engineering-manager-developer-ecosystem-amsterdam-300494","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794639323},{"slug":"engineering-manager-developer-ecosystem-amsterdam-107355","company_name":"databricks","title":"Engineering Manager - Developer Ecosystem","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;RDQ427R369&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
