g layer (e.g. dbt) that serves as the single source of truth for analysts, data scientists and self-serving PMs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead data governance: define and enforce event naming and tracking standards, a schema change process, documentation, and dashboard ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed privacy in the data stack: make sure personal data is categorized, minimized and pseudonymized before it reaches downstream and third-party tools, in close collaboration with Legal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the health of the stack: monitoring, alerting, data quality checks and cost management, so issues are caught before they reach stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define who owns what across our data tooling (e.g. Mixpanel, our warehouse and BI layer), and help teams get the most out of self-serve analytics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable data enrichment to unlock deeper insights for Product and Growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore how we can safely use LLMs (such as Claude) on top of our data for analysis and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the go-to data partner for Product, Engineering and Growth, and help grow the data function as Polarsteps scales.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>The equipment in your backpack</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What we're hoping you'll bring with you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ 5+ years of experience in data engineering, analytics engineering or a hybrid data role, ideally in a B2C product or mobile app company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Strong SQL and Python, and hands-on experience modeling large event datasets in a modern warehouse (e.g. ClickHouse, Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Experience with dbt and an orchestration tool such as Airflow or Dagster.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Proven track record of bringing structure to data governance: tracking plans, event ownership, documentation and data quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Experience with product analytics tools (e.g. Mixpanel, Amplitude) and BI tools (e.g. Metabase, Looker).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Comfortable owning infrastructure decisions: cloud (AWS/GCP/Azure), infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform), CI/CD for data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ A pragmatic, ownership-driven mindset: you're happy to set the strategy and get your hands dirty, and you enjoy the hygiene work others tend to avoid.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Excellent communication skills: you can explain trade-offs to engineers and to non-technical stakeholders alike.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong> Bonus points if you have:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Experience with mobile attribution or marketing data (e.g. AppsFlyer, SKAdNetwork, ad platform APIs).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Experience with reverse ETL or CDPs (e.g. RudderStack, Twilio Segment).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Experience with experimentation data and A/B testing infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✨ </strong>Knowledge of GDPR and handling personal data responsibly in an analytics stack.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>1st class Polarsteps extras</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Some cool things to make the journey extra sweet.</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A yearly free flight or train ride to a random location! Give our Teleporter a spin <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.polarsteps.com/teleporter">here.</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A shiny MacBook to work your magic on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working, our way. Work from home <em>and</em> the office, we ask everyone to be in the office 2 days a week. It’s how we stay flexible, focused, and meaningfully