p and be rewarded for the value they bring. That's why we build software that helps organizations set clear expectations, define what a role entails, assess performance fairly, support employee growth and make compensation transparent and explainable. From clear roles to fair rewards, all within one continuous process.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We do this with a driven team of 55+ colleagues. Hundreds of companies in the Netherlands, from scale-ups to corporates, already use Learned. Now we're taking the next step: </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Germany</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Senior Partnership Manager Germany</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> you're part of our founding DE team. You build the partner channel from scratch and become the face of Learned in the German HR ecosystem.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Lay the foundation for our partner channel in Germany</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">You build our German partner channel from the ground up. You decide how we do partnerships in Germany, and then you make it happen: from the first partner to a network that brings in a steady flow of new business.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Our network has two parts:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Implementation partners:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> HR consultants and advisory firms that bring Learned to their clients.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Learning partners:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> </span>companies specialized in job evaluation and learning &amp; development.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">What you’ll do</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Set the strategy.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Map the German HR ecosystem and decide which partners to focus on first. Set clear targets for the channel and make sure partners and direct sales strengthen each other.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Build the foundation.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Shape the partner model for Germany: partner tiers, the commercial terms, and the playbook and processes that let the channel grow. Our Dutch partner programme is your starting point. You adapt it to the German market.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Find and close new partners.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Start conversations at board level, then negotiate and close partnerships.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Turn partners into growth.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Onboard and enable partners, build joint plans and turn them into a steady source of new business.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Activate the market.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Put Learned on the map in Germany with partner and customer events, such as roundtables, webinars and breakfast sessions. You work together with marketing and get operational support for running them.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">How your time is split (at the start)</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~50%: Finding new partners</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~30%: Partner management</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~10%: Events and activation</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">~10%: Strategy</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">As the network grows, your focus shifts towards partner management and scaling the channel. You might also build a team around it.</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you work with</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You report to our Partnership Lead in NL and work closely with our Founding Account Executive Germany..</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Where you'll work</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">You choose one of two setups:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Based in or around Düsseldorf or Cologne.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You work remotely in North Rhine-Westphalia, close to your partners and visit our office in Utrecht regularly. We plan to open an office in Düsseldorf or Cologne, and you'll help build it.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Based in or around Utrecht (NL).</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You work from our office in Utrecht and travel to the NRW region about </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">twice a month for a few days</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Either way, you start with an onboarding at our office in Utrecht.</span></p> <br> <h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you are</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A bachelor's or master's level of thinking and working</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">At least </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">8 years of experience</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> in business development, partnerships, sales or account management, ideally in SaaS or HR tech</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A track record of building partner channels or new markets from scratch</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An existing network in the German HR, consulting or HR-tech ecosystem is a big plus</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Native German speaker</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> and fluent in English. Dutch is a plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You're an entrepreneurial hunter: you open doors, talk easily at board level and close deals on your own</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You're organised, think strategically and keep the overview while doing the hands-on work</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You have an affinity with HR, learning &amp; development or technology</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">What we offer</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">We're ambitious and entrepreneurial, and we take steps towards our big goals together every day. Having fun matters just as much. You get:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">€70,000 – €80,000 base salary and €90,000 – €100,000 OTE</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> gross per year</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A rare chance to be part of our founding team in Germany and shape the market from day one</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A local employment contract in Germany through our employer of record partner (or a Dutch contract if you're based in the Netherlands)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A MacBook and everything you need to do your job well</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">25 vacation days (full-time)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Travel allowance and travel costs for your trips to Germany or the Netherlands</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A personal development budget of €1,000 per year</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An ambitious, international team with 7+ nationalities, where we keep each other sharp and celebrate successes</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">When you're in Utrecht: a daily (healthy) lunch with the team and a fun team activity every month</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p