partments to ensure we are not just winning business, but building long-term value and market share.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own top of the funnel activity for a dedicated region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hit conversion targets across the stages of the funnel that are in your responsibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate our value and mission to our prospective partners, build trusted relationships with the hospitality network in the region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do market research and competition analysis to identify opportunities within your region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Ops, Product, and Leadership to remove bottlenecks and improve scaling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure smooth handoff to Success following close to drive activation and ongoing performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain high CRM hygiene to enable the best handover to the sales and success team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">0-1 years of experience in Sales, Sales Operations or Customer-facing roles ideally within SaaS/ Tech/ Hospitality or Startup space.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion for the hospitality industry and customer-facing activities is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree in business, finance, engineering, or a related field (or equivalent work experience) is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to roll up your sleeves and “Leave your ego at the door” mentality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced startup environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to effectively engage with customers and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial mindset: you thrive in fast-moving environments, love building from scratch, and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ideal candidate will be fluent in English and Dutch</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this speaks to you we can be the right fit. Learn more about how we work from our Recipe here:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers"> <u>https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch Provided in Office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team events</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we use AI at Tebi</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or